 have a practice battle."&\rMisty: Good luck with your gym."\bPrimeape".Would you like to take Primeape with you?"Yes"NoIu;␀�'[[�"O\bMy head hurts trying to think about how to get through the challenges..."W\bDo I need high damaging moves? Or should I weaken them with tricks and statuses?"Y\bOr maybe I need to my Pokémons' EVs... or even worse, hunting high IV Pokémon..."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the DUET CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"8\bAnd what difficulty will you be participating in?"\bSure." \rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN!".\rWould you like to recieve some healing?"\r... and done! Ta-da!"o\rCan't believe you made me fully restore your team, you bastard. This wasn't supposed to even be a thing."`\rWhat, you expected a full heal? Haha, don't be ridiculous. This is already very generous."9\rYour team should already be at full health, right?"8\rHope you will have a good time in Sync Challenge!"1\bChoose your entrance. \ch[73,,A,B,C,D,E,F]")\bHmph, if this were a fist fight..."Q\bHi, this is the entrance for the TITAN CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"z\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Sync Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)")\bLuc-ker: You want some tips? Sure."�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto, Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary, Neo Champion,Sygna Buffs]"�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto,Johto, Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary,Neo Champion]"!\bGood luck, you'll need it."�\bAnd don't worry if you lose, you'll still get GC Credits for trying! That is, if you don't hit F12 because you're a sore loser or a tryhard."�\bYou want some general tips? Hmm. Best tip I can give here is to expect the unexpected. They don't play by the meta of the main series game, they play by PoMas's meta."�\bFor example, they'll buff their stats up by a lot more than they probably should, invent new mechanics, ignore Protect and heal more than they should, just to name a few things."�\bThey'll also have some interesting moves too, ranging from moves used by their trainers instead or powerful moves that can only be used under certain conditions."�\bFuthermore, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"�\bBut lastly, and you might find a silver lining in this - I've made it so that not only do you benefit from some damage reduction, the "harder" trainers have a lower chance to show up early."�\bSo if you want to familiarise yourself with the trainers here, it might be good to try this challenge with a lower difficulty first.".\bIn any case, good luck, you'll need it."�\bSure. Which one would you like me to explain? \ch[1,-1,Crit Rate,Trainer Move,B Move,Passive Skill, Master Passive,Zone,Gradual Healing]"R\bCrit Rate - how often a Pokémon lands a crit, up to a maximum of 3 stages."�\bTrainer Move - A move that the trainer uses (rather than their Pokémon). These moves tend to buff the user's Pokémon or their team's side."^\bThey can be used even when the trainer's Pokémon is afflicted with a status condition."}\bB Move - Stands for Buddy Move. You can identify them by the "descriptor" in the move's name, e.g. Origin Volt Tackle."~\bThey tend to do what the move they're based on does, but with increased power, added effects or the regular effect enhanced."\bThere's usually a condition that has to be met before each B Move can be used, so use that to your advantage to counter them!"�\bIf they don't, they will likely have very little PP instead. Lastly, all trainers only have 1 B Move at most, but there is 1 exception."mPassive Skill - Essentially an extra ability, but they can't be ignored by effects such as Mold Breaker."~\bHow many a Pokémon has is completely arbitrary, though I've tried to limit it to 3 at most, excluding Master Passives."l\bMaster Passive - A Passive Skill that increases the team's damage dealt and reduces the damage taken."k\bThere are 3 types: Flag Bearer is for all moves and is 10% damage increase and 20% damage reduction."W\bPride is for physical moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."_\bLastly, Spirit is for special moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."`\bZone - A field effect like a weather or terrain, boosting moves of a certain type by 50%."s\bGradual Healing - The Pokémon recovers 1/16th of their max HP every turn. Think of it kinda like Leftovers."T\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Brock,Misty,Erika, Red,Red (Thunderbolt),Blue,Leaf]"W\bBrock probably has the most basic kit here, since he's PoMas's first Sygna Suit."�\bAnyway, his Trainer Move give his Tyranitar's +1 Defense and makes its next attack guaranteed to land and crit, but there are ways to get around it, like Protect."�\bTtar has 2 passives. One gives its moves a higher chance to apply their additional effects and the other prevents its stats from dropping in a sandstorm."s\bMisty also has a very basic kit. Her Trainer Move gives her Vaporeon +2 Defense and her side +2 Sp. Defense."�\bLastly, her Vaporeon's passives give it gradual healing when switching in as well as a chance to raise its Evasion after it uses a move."}\bErika's Trainer Move gives her Leafeon's +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, but if the Sun's up, these stat increases are doubled."`\bLeafeon's ability is Chorophyll, so with the Sun up, her Leafeon's speed will be doubled."t\bThen, its passives don't allow status conditions to be inflicted on it as well as heal it after using a move."@\bIn other words, you really don't want Leafeon in the Sun!"�\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Charizard's +3 Attack, Sp. Attack and Speed and +2 Crit Rate, though its Defense and Sp. Defense are lowered by -1."{\bHis Charizard also has passives which allow its moves to never miss and not require a rechage turn after using them."X\bKnow what that means? It's able to use Blast Burn. Every. Single. Turn. Have fun!"s\bRed actually has a second Sygna Suit in PoMas. His Trainer Move gives Pikachu +6 Attack and Gradual Healing."�\bPikachu can also Gigantamax, though it maxes less use of it here compared to PoMas, since there you only use 1 Dynamax move for each sync pair per battle."h\bIt also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."{\bIts other passives make all its moves critical hits, as well as healing it after it uses a move in Electric Terrain."q\bLast, but certainly not least, Pikachu has a B Move which can only be used when Electric Terrain's active."X\bIf your Pokémon's paralyzed, its Defense and Sp. Defense are also lowered by -1."r\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Defense and +1 Crit Rate, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."~\bAnyway, his Blastoise is a tank of all time. When it's hit, one of its passive gives his side +1 Attack and Sp. Attack."�\bAnd then when it attacks, its other passive gives its side +1 Sp. Defense. Lastly, it also doesn't need to recharge after using Hydro Cannon."`\bWith Leaf's Trainer Move, I took a few creative liberties to make it live up to its name."q\bIt provides the Pokémon on her side Gradual Healing, as well as healing them all for 40% of their max HP!"�\bAs for Venusaur's passives, they badly poison your Pokémon and gives them -1 to their defensive stats after they're attacked by it."h\bWith Razor Leaf and a non-recharging Frenzy Plant, it's sure to deal out a ton poison and damage."Y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Morty,Ethan,Lyra,Kris, Silver,Giovanni,Giovanni (Ultra)]"q\bMorty's Trainer Move gives +1 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate to his side, as well as setting Tailwind."�\bOne of Ho-oh's passives gives additional stat boosts to its team if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."a\bIts other passive then heals the Pokémon on Ho- oh's side when it uses a move in the Sun."s\bEthan's Trainer Move powers up Lugia's next special move, gives it +1 Accuracy and makes its next move crit."{\bLugia has passives which makes its single target attacks hit all opponents as well as restore PP to Ethan's Trainer Move."k\bLastly, it also has a Spirit Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bLyra's Trainer Move gives +2 Attack and Sp. Attack to a Pokémon on her side and gives them Gradual Healing. But that's not the crazy thing about this sync pair."�\bCelebi has passives which leaves the opponent flinched, trapped and confused after using a move and lowers one of the target's stats by -2."v\bAnnnnd Celebi has Grassy Glide and can set up Grassy Terrain too to give it priority. Talk about a nasty combo!"j\bLastly, it also has a Pride Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."N\bIf you face her, pray that the other sync pairs are physical attackers."O\bAt base, her Trainer Move gives her side +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate."{\bBut if it's Raining, it also powers up the next special attack from her team, making them pack an even bigger punch."�\bOne of Suicune's passives gives its side +4 Sp. Defense if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."�\bIts other passive heals its team after a uses a move under the Rain. I think you get the idea - Rain is dangerous if you're facing Kris!"k\bLastly, it has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."k\bSilver's Trainer Move gives Sneasel +3 Attack and Speed, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."�\bSneasel's B Move, Crushing Tripel Axel, can only be used when its HP is full. In theory, that doesn't sound too hard to counter, right?"\bWell, on every hit of a multi-hit move, its passives lower the opposing Pokémon's Speed by -1 while it gets +1 Evasion."~\bIt also gets +1 Crit Rate on each hit of its B Move too, but it doesn't have any other ways of increasing its damage itself."N\bSo at best, you get lucky and OHKO it, while at worst, it's a nuisance."<\bGiovanni's Trainer Move gives his Nidoking +6 Attack."a\bHis Nidoking has a passive to make all its attacks critical hits, including its Max Moves."�\bIts other passive turns Normal moves into Ground moves, allowing it to gain STAB from it. Its Mega Kick is going to hit pretty hard!"�\bThis version of Giovanni has a Trainer Move which gives his side +2 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as making Guzzlord the center of attention."{\bGuzzlord has passives which enable its Stockpile Defense and Sp. Defense boosts to be tripled and shared with its allies."O\bHowever, it can only Stockpile a maximum of 2 times as a result of this."�\bGuzzlord also doesn't have just 1 B Move, but 2! It's the one exception to the "rule" that says there can only be 1 B Move for each sync pair."i\bWhen used, they both remove Stockpiles's stat boosts and restores 1 PP to Giovanni's Trainer Move."�\bThe first one, Guzzling Swallow, can only be used after Stockpile has been used and restores Guzzlord's HP based on how many times it was used."=\bThen, it restores a fixed amount of HP for its allies."�\bThe second one is Gourging Crunch. It can only be used when the Guzzlord's stat boosts for Defense and Sp. Defense are 6 or greater."9\bIt then lowers the target's defensive stats by -1.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,May,Brendan,Steven,Wally]"�\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Blaziken +4 Attack and +1 Accuracy, sets up Tailwind and protects it from damage for the rest of the turn."�\bBlaziken's first passive gives +1 Speed to its side when entering battle, including Mega Evolution, effectively translating to a +2 increase."�\bIts other passive lowers the target's Defense by -2. All in all, very speedy and it can easily snowball if you're not careful."c\bBrendan's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense as well as +1 Crit Rate."u\bHis Latios's first passive powers up its sides' next special moves when entering the battle and Mega Evolving."x\bIts other passive then increases the likelihood of additional effects; if it's a stat drop, it'll be doubled too."p\bIt has Luster Purge, so that'll mean that you'll be taking a lot of special damage if you're not careful!"�\bSteven... is a lot. Because he has a Deoxys, PoMas decided to give him not just 1 form of Deoxys, but all 4! So let's break him down a bit.\ch[2,-1,Initial State,Shared Traits, Normal Forme,Attack Forme,Defense Forme,Speed Forme]"\bInitially, Deoxys starts in its Normal Forme with 4 Trainer Moves and a passive which gives it +1 Accuracy when switching in."�\bThe first one, "Try This!", sets Psychic Terrain and gives Deoxys +2 Defense, Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Speed and keep Deoxys in its Normal Forme."u\bHis second one, "Attack!", gives Deoxys +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, then changes Deoxys into Attack Forme."�\bThe third one, "Defend!" gives its +4 side Attack and Sp. Attack. Deoxys then changes into its Defense Form and protects itself from damage for the rest of the turn."r\bLast but not least,"Faster!", gives Deoxys +6 Speed and +3 Evasion and changes Deoxys into its Speed Forme."�\bOutside of its inital state, all forms of Deoxys that Steven has have a passive with converts stat drops into stat increases, but not vice versa like Contrary does!"a\bThey all also have Psycho Boost and Zen Headbutt, so I won't be mentioning them elsewhere."`\bIn its Normal Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."{\bIt also has a passive which increase the chance of additional effects, so if it uses Zen Headbutt, be prepared to flinch!"`\bIn its Attack Forme, Deoxys has Protect and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which increases the power of its next physical and special moves, so it might quickly snowball out of control!"a\bIn its Defense Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Iron Defense in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which gives its side +2 Sp. Defense each time a status move is used, so with Iron Defense it'll become very bulky very quickly."^\bIn its Speed Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Double Team in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which sets up Tailwind for its side when a status move is successful the first time it's used in battle."_\bWally's Trainer Move gives his Gardevoir +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Sp. Defense and Crit Rate."�\bGardevoir has 2 passives - the first gives its side +1 Speed when entering battle and Mega Evolving; the other leaves the target confused after a move."�\bGardevoir also has a B Move, Ultimate Dazzling Gleam. It lowers the targets' Attack and Sp. Attack by -4, then makes them weaker to Fairy type attacks."�\bIt can only be used once, but you can't Protect against it and -4 on your attacking stats will likely force you to switch out your Pokémon."V\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Cynthia,Cynthia (Renegade),Cynthia (Aura),Cyrus,Dawn]"�\bCynthia's Trainer Move, which I took some creative liberties with, raises her Kommo-o's Crit Rate and boosts its next special attack depending on how low its HP is."�\bApart from that, Kommo-o has passives which allow it to ignore damage reduction from Reflect, Light Screen and Aurora Veil as well as increase the chance for additional effects."�\bThis version of Cynthia's Trainer Move gives Giratina +4 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate. She can also set a Ghost Zone."T\bHer Giratina's attacks lower the Defense and Sp. Defense of the target by -1."�\bThis Cynthia's Trainer Move gives her side +4 Defense and Sp. Defense, but if a Fighting Zone is active, she'll give +6 instead."r\bAs for that, her Lucario has a passive which sets Fighting Zone on entry, so most of the time, it'll be +6."s\bLucario's other passive also depends on Fighting Zone - it heals its side after using a move if it's active."y\bIt also has Superior Aura Sphere, a B Move that never misses and can only be used after Lucario is attacked twice."]\bAfter it deals damage, it powers up the next physical and special attacks of its side."p\bLastly, Lucario has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."\bCyrus's Trainer Move gives his Darkrai +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy and Crit Rate. In addition, he can set a Dark Zone."�\bDarkrai has passives which power up its moves if the target is asleep, or if it's using a status move, it'll lower a random stat of all opponents by -1."[\bIt does have Dark Void, but even if it misses, its 2nd passive will activate anyway."�\bDawn's Trainer Move gives her side +2 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate, but her Cresslia takes recoil damage equal to 30% of its remaining HP."^\bYou might be thinking, why do that, when most other trainer moves don't have downsides?"i\bCresselia's very tanky, but one of its passives makes it even more so when it has 50% HP or lower."�\bIts other passive also increases the power of its side's special moves if Cresselia uses a status move when it's HP is 50% or lower."P\bIt also has Moonlight for healing, so don't count your chickens too soon!"R\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Elesa,Grimsley,Hilbert,Hilda,N, Roxie,Ingo,Emmet]"�\bElesa's Trainer Move gives +2 Accuracy and Crit Rate to a Pokémon on her side, as well as giving +2 Sp. Attack to all Pokémon on her side."�\bRotom has a passive which gives it +1 Evasion when it's hit, as well as another which prevents its Evasion from being lowered."�\bGrimsley's Trainer Move makes his Sharpedo take recoil damage equal to 90% of its remaining HP, but in return it gives +6 Attack and Evasion and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition, it has passives which increase the chance of the additional effects its moves and increase their power when Sharpedo is in a pinch."s\bHilbert's Trainer Move gives his Genesect +3 Sp. Attack, +2 Crit Rate and powers up its next special attack."�\bWhen using Techno Blast, Genesect changes form depending on the type the target is weakest to. Its default is also Bug instead of Normal."]\bThen, it makes them weaker to that type and applies an effect corresponding that type."m\bElectric - Paralyze target.\n Fire - Lower target's Attack by -1.\n Ice - 50% chance to freeze target."H\bWater - Lower target's Defense by -1. Bug - No additional effect."d\bLastly, if Genesect lands a super effective hit, its passive lowers the target's Speed by -2."�\bHilda's Trainer Move raises her Victini's Sp. Attack by how much its Attack has been raised, then gives it +3 Crit Rate and gives its team +1 Accuracy."�\bThis is complemented by Victini's passives, which gives it +2 Attack on switching in and turns stat drops into stat increases."y\bThere's even more synergy - Victini has V-Create, so it just keeps getting bulkier and faster each time it's used!"D\bN's Trainer Move gives his Kyurem +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bWhen Kyurem uses charges up to use Freeze Shock, it has a passive which halves the damage it takes while charging and unlocks its B Move, Resonating Noble Roar."|\bIt lowers the Attack, Sp. Attack, and Speed of all opposing Pokémon by -2, while it powering up its next physical attack."�\bFreeze Shock then needs to be used again before it can be used again, preventing it from being spammed endlessly (it also has 3 PP)."�\bKyurem also has a passive which allows it to ignore the opponent's enduring effects, but I imagine that won't come up too often."q\bRoxie's Trainer Move gives her Toxtricity +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate and applies Tailwind to her side."W\bToxtricity has has 2 passives. One sets Poison Zone on switch in and extends it."e\bThe other lowers the target's Attack or Sp. Attack if it's poisoned or paralyzed respectively."~\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Frenzied Sludge Wave. It can only be used if there's an opponent with a status condition."�\bIt can't be protected against, lowers the target's Sp. Defense by -2 and poisons it if it doesn't already have a status condition."^\bIngo's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. His Chandelure can Dynamax."�\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as increasing the power of its team's next special moves."�\bIt also has a B Move, Rising Flames Hex. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."�\bIt applies effects based on what the target's inflicted with:\nParalysis - Lower target's Defense by -2.\n Burn - Lower target's Sp. Defense by -2."^\bPoison - Heal itself and allies for a little HP.\n Flinch - Lower target's Speed by -2."b\bTrap - Power up user's next physical move.\n Confusion - Power up user's next special move."�\bEmmet's Trainer Move gives a Pokémon on his side Ground immunity for 5 turns and makes its next moves critical hits. His Eelektross can Dynamax."m\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as trapping the target."�\bIt also has a B Move, Descending Lightning Wild Charge. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."A\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Korrina,Diantha,Lysandre]"g\bSerena's Trainer Move gives her +6 Zygarde's Attack and Sp. Attack and gives it Gradual Healing."\\bZygarde's passives prevent its stats from being lowered and its attacks from missing."p\bLastly, it also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bKorrina's Trainer Move gives her Marshadow +4 Attack and +3 Speed and Evasion. After attacking, Marshadow's passive raises one of its stats by +1 3 times."|\bIf her Diancie's Defense has been raised, Diantha's Trainer Move raises its Sp. Defense by the same amount of stages."`\bThen, it gives Diancie Gradual Healing and makes its next physical attack do more damage."x\bDiancie's B Move, Pink Diamond Storm, can only be used when there's a Rock Zone active, which Diantha can set up."M\bIt lowers the target's Defense by -2 while giving its side +2 Defense."�\bDiancie's passives lower all opponents' Speed by -1 when entering battle and Mega Evolving, as well as giving it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate after using a move."_\bLysandre's Trainer Move gives his +4 Volcanion Sp. Attack, +1 Accuracy and +3 Crit Rate."�\bVolcanion itself has one passive which burns the targets that it hits. This is then complimented with its B Move, Heat Hydro Pump."�\bIt can only be used when at least one opposing Pokémon is burned and is an AoE move which deals more damage to burned targets."o\bThen, based on how many burned targets it hits, it makes Volcanion's next special attack do more damage."I\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lusamine,Hau,Lana, Acerola,Mina,Gladion]"v\bLusamine's Trainer Move gives Necrozma +6 Sp. Attack and -1 Speed. Her Dusk-Mane Necrozma can also Ultra Burst."�\bIt also has passives which turns its single target moves into AoE moves and allows Prismatic Laser to be used without the user recharging."M\bHau's Trainer Move gives his Tapu Koko +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."z\bWhen entering battle, one of Koko's passives extends the duration of the Electric Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next special attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."l\bThen, Koko's B Move, Wild Electroweb, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt doubles in power when a Fairy Zone is active (which Hau can set up) and lowers the Speed of all targets by -2 while +2 Speed to Koko and its allies."H\bLana's Trainer Move gives her Tapu Lele +6 Attack and Sp. Attack."y\bWhen entering battle, one of Lele's passives extends the duration of the Psychic Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up its next physical and special attacks when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."{\bLastly, its B Move, Neo Psycho Cut, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It always crits."�\bAcerola's Trainer Move gives +2 Defense and +3 Crit Rate to her side's Pokémon. If it's Sunny (which her Tapu Bulu can set up), it gives +2 Attack too."v\bWhen entering battle, Bulu's first passive extends the duration of the Grassy Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next physical attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."t\bLastly, its B Move, Unbreakable Swords Dance, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."b\bIt gives +2 Attack to Bulu and its allies makes their next physical attacks do more damage."�\bMina's Trainer Move sets up Lucky Chant on her side and gives +4 Sp. Attack (+6 if Raining) and Gradual Healing to the Pokémon on her side."x\bWhen entering battle, Tapu Fini's ability sets Fairy Zone (because Misty Terrain sucks) and extends its duration."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which gives its side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."p\bLastly, Fini's B Move, Sea Deity Protect, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt applies Protect to itself and its allies, then it restores 20% HP (30% with Fairy Zone) for itself and its allies and returns lowered stats back to normal if it's Raining."q\bGladion's Trainer Move gives his Magearna +6 Sp. Attack, +3 Crit Rate and powers up its next special move."�\bMagearna has passives which lower the target's Sp. Attack by -2 after using a move and prevent its own stats from being lowered."]\bThen, Magearna's B Move, Piercing Fleur Cannon, can only be used after it uses a move."}\bIts power and the power of its next special move increases based on how much the targets' Sp. Attack has been lowered.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Leon,Piers,Gloria (Dojo)]"o\bLeon's Trainer Move gives his Eternatus +3 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate but lowers its Sp. Defense by -1."�\bHis Eternatus is also able to Eternamax and one of its passives enables its Eternabeam to not require a recharge turn after it's used."~\bIts other passive also lowers the target's Attack, Defense, Sp. Attack, Sp. Defense, Speed, Accuracy and Evasion by -1."O\bPier's Trainer Move gives his Toxtricity +2 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."�\bToxtricity has passives which set Electric Terrain and extend it on switch in, as well as ignore the target's enduring effects."}\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Sorrowful Echos Overdrive. It can only be used if there's an active weather, terrain or zone."�\bIt also can't be protected against and does more damage if the target has a status condition, which would most likely happen from its Sludge Bomb."Z\bGloria's Trainer Move gives her Urshifu +3 Attack. Her Urshifu can also Gigantamax."p\bOther than that, it just has passives which lower the target's Defense and Speed by -1 when hitting them."j\bWith Surging Strikes, it'll apply to each hit, so you'll actually end up with -3 Defense and Speed!"v\bNice choice! These guys were made for PoMas's anniversaries and are much simpler compared to the Neo Champions."m\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lillie (2022),N (2022),Steven (2022), May (2023),Skyla (2023),Raihan (2023)]"l\bFun fact: This is my favourite anniversary trainer out of them all! Her skirt is sooo good... anyway!"m\bLillie's Trainer Move gives her Lunala +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, the first of its kind in PoMas."b\bIts passives set Tailwind when its switched in and powers up its moves when its HP is full."r\bN's Trainer Move gives his Reshiram +3 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy, as well as setting Tailwind on his side."v\bIts passives turn its single target moves into AoE moves and lower the target's Sp. Defense after attacking it."K\bSteven's Trainer Move gives his Rayquaza +2 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."a\bIts passives turn stat drops into stat increases and gives it +1 Speed after using a move."{\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Latias +2 Defense and Sp. Defense and +3 Crit Rate, as well as setting Tailwind on her side."s\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and doubles stat drops that it inflicts."s\bSkyla's Trainer Move gives her Tornadus +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as giving her side +2 Speed."v\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and confuses the target after attacking it."�\bRaihan's Trainer Move gives his Flygon +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate, then powers up his team's next physical and special moves."�\bIts passives power up its team's next physical and special moves when using a status move and when attacking a target that's flinching, trapped or confused, it lowers its attacking stats by -1."&\bLastly, his Flygon can Dynamax."n\bHoho! All of these guys have a Master Passive (I'm assuming you know what that is by now) and a B Move."y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Calem,Marnie, Hop,Bede,Red,Leaf,Blue,Nate,Rosa,Silver,Cheren, Bianca,May,Brendan]"w\bSerena has quite a lot going on, so let's split her kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"n\bSerena is quite interesting. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."\bThe simplest part of her kit is definitely her Trainer Move. It gives her Greninja +2 Attack, +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."5\bHer Greninja also has a Spirit Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which max out the number of hits of a multi-strike move and for each hit, it lowers a random stat of the target by -1."T\bThat means its Water Shuriken will always end up lowering your stats 5 times!"z\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which lower the target's Accuracy by -1 and has a chance of making it flinch."b\bBoundless Quick Attack won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"�\bIt makes the target weaker to Greninja's current type, as well as lower its Defense and Sp. Defense by -2 and give its side +3 Speed."v\bCalem has quite a lot going on, so let's split his kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"g\bCalem is pretty cool. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."�\bThe simplest part of his kit is definitely his Trainer Move. It gives his side +4 Attack, +2 Sp. Attack and Crit Rate, then sets up Tailwind."4\bHis Greninja also has a Pride Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to status conditions, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in the rain."�\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to stat drops, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in a Dark Zone."h\bTransformational Double Team won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"c\bWhen Greninja's a Water type, it'll make it rain and power up its side's next special moves."i\bIf it's a Dark type, it'll set up a Dark Zone and power up its side's next physical moves instead."S\bThen regardless of type, it'll also give Greninja and its allies +2 Evasion."�\bMarnie's Trainer Move gives her Galarian Moltres +6 Sp. Attack, +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. It then takes 10% of its max HP as recoil damage."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives give it +3 Crit Rate when switching in and powers up its moves when it's not at max HP."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fierce Fiery Wrath, can only be used after 2 other moves have been used. It can't be protected against and flinchest its target(s)."q\bHop's Trainer Move gives his Galarian Zapdos +3 Speed and -1 Sp. Defense. It then sets up a Fighting Zone."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives give it +2 Attack on entry and lower the target's Sp. Defense when lowering its Defense."�\bLastly, its B Move, Roaring Thunderous Kick, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It lowers the target's Defense by -3."�\bBede's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Attack, Sp. Attack and Crit Rate, as well as powering up his side's next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives give its side +1 Speed on entry and makes it immune to critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Intimidating Freezing Glare, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It gives his side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."i\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Kantonian Articuno +6 Sp. Attack and powers up its next special move."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, it has quite a few other passives. First off, its moves will always land and be critical hits."�\bThen, it lowers its target's resistance to ice moves and powers up its next special attack based on how many opponents its move hit."�\bLastly, its B Move, Frozen Wings Ice Beam, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type and freezes the target."a\bLeaf's Trainer Move gives her Kantonian Moltres +6 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."Z\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its passives supercharge its status moves."�\bIn addition to their original effects, it makes them lower the target's Attack, Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense by -1 and makes it weaker to Fire moves."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fiery Wings Flare Blitz, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type. It burns the target and double its stat drops."z\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as powering up their next special moves."^\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its passives make its moves very potent."�\bIn addition to their original effects, they make the target weaker to Electric moves and give Zapdos's side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."r\bLastly, its B Move, Thundering Wings Roost, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type."�\bIt heals Zapdos and its allies for 60% and 30% of their respective max HPs, gives its side Gradual Healing and removes all their status conditions."d\bNate's Trainer Move returns his Haxorus's lowered stats back to normal and gives it +3 Speed."~\bWith Nate using his Trainer Move, one of Haxorus's passives will also give it +6 Attack and power up its next physical move."`\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passive makes its moves critical hits."f\bLastly, its B Move, Dark Black Outrage, can only be used when Haxorus's Attack has been raised."�\bRosa's Trainer Move gives her side a boost to her team's special or physical moves when Meloetta is in its Aria or Pirouette forms respectively."}\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives play around the fact that Meloetta has 2 different forms."U\bFirst off, its Normal moves become the same type as Meloetta's secondary type."�\bAfter using a move, it then give its side +1 Defense or Sp. Defense (Pirouette and Aria respectively) and makes its target weaker to Meloetta's second type."p\bLastly, its B Move, Relic Song of Wonder, can only be used when Meloetta is at 1/3 or more of its max HP."�\bIt changes Meloetta's form and powers up its side's next physical and special moves and has a chance to make the target fall asleep."{\bSilver's Trainer Move gives his Tyranitar +6 Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as +1 Accuracy if used in a Sandstorm."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives strengthen it in a Sandstorm. First, it extends the duration of Sandstorms."\bIts moves also get powered up in a Sandstorm and it also gets a boost to its next physical attack after using an attack."�\bLastly, its B Move, Massive Rock Slide, always flinches its target(s) but can't be used consecutively or on Ttar's first turn in battle."�\bCheren's Trainer Move gives his Tornadus +4 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as powering it its next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives make its moves always land, be critical hits, then strengthen its next physical and special moves."y\bLastly, its B Move, Black Gale Bleakwind Storm, can't be used consecutively or on Tornadus's first turn in battle."}\bIt increases in power based on how much its next physical move would be powered up and lower the target's Speed by -2."}\bIn addition, if it's used as Tornadus's 2nd move after entering battle, it makes the target(s) weaker to Flying moves."K\bBianca's Trainer Move gives her Virizion +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives allow gives its side +1 Speed and Evasion after using a move and ignore enduring."�\bLastly, its B Move, White Light Sacred Sword, lowers the target's attacking stats by -3 and makes its weaker to Fighting moves."A\bIt also ignores the target's defensive and evasive boosts."�\bMay's Trainer Move powers up the next special move of a Pokémon on her side and her Kyogre, as well as giving the latter +2 Sp. Attack."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Sp. Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Blue Origin Pulse, can only be used in Heavy Rain. It lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Sp. Defense by -3."�\bBrendan's Trainer Move powers up the next physical move of a Pokémon on his side and his Groudon, as well as giving the latter +2 Attack."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."v\bLastly, its B Move, Red Precipice Blades, lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Defense by -2."v\bHowever, it can only be used in Harsh Sun and can't be used consecutively or on Groudon's first turn in battle."z\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Sync Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bEssentially, you have 7 energy worth of buffs. There are 5 types of buffs: Blessings, Immunities, Restoration, Boosters and Crushers."q\bWhat buff type would you like to know about? \ch[1,-1,Blessings,Immunities,Restoration,Boosters, Crushers]"\bBlessings give your Pokémon stat increases at the start of a battle and they use energy corresponding with their level."�\bIn addition, you can buy an enhanced version of the buff (apart from the Assasin's Blessing) for just a few more of your hard-earned credits."�\bAs an example, Warrior's Blessing Lv. 1 will give your Pokémon +1 Attack when they enter battle, essentially giving them Intrepid Sword!"�\bImmunites make your Pokémon immune to status conditions, "interferences" (i.e. flinching, trapping and confusion) or even critical hits for some time."Q\bAll of them use 2 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."�\bHowever, once you buy out the whole store, you can then buy buffs that make you immune to all status conditions and interferences."<\bThey will use up 4 and 3 energy respectively, though."�\bIf you talk to Nurse Joy now, she'll actually heal your team now! But... just a little bit, if you don't give her any energy. Better than nothing though, amirite?"�\bAt base, she'll heal your team for 10% of its HP, as well as restore 1/8 of its PP (restoring at least 1 PP per move, though)."�\bThe restoration buffs increase those amounts though. For each level of the HP Recovery buff, she'll heal 25%, 50% and 100% of your team's HP."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your 'mons alive!"m\bFor each level of the PP Recovery buff, it'll restore 1/4, 1/2 and all of your team's PP respectively."�\bFurthermore, she also won't remove status conditions from your team; you'll have to equip the Status Recovery buff first! It costs 3 energy."�\bLastly, these buffs are only active in the Sync Challenge. If she gave any healing in the Titan Challenge, it would be wayyy too easy!"}\bBoosters give your Pokémon +1 to a stat (except Accuracy and Evasion) after they use a move, even if the move failed."Q\bAll of them use 1 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."l\bCrushers lowers one of the target's stats (except Accuracy and Evasion) by -1 after they're attacked."f\bAlso, they won't be effective in Titan Challenge; all opponents there are immune to stat drops."9\bI wish I could join the Fire Ash Discord Events..."`\bThrough those events, I could win high IV boosts or maybe rare shinies and legendaries..."\bShucks..."N\bI might have lost.... But my determination is still burning high!!!!!!!"A\rNurse Joy: Looks like your Pokémon need some patching up."R\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Get ready and take care now!"L\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Better luck next time!"\bOut of bounds, kiddo!"*\rThese challenges are an eye opener."]\rThat towering Inferno, shivering Sheer Cold. An overwhelming Draco Meteor coming next."R\rWhere do these trainers come from? Whoa... I wish I could be like them too.":\rConcierge Joi: Welcome to the Secret Grandeur Club!"\\rComing from other dimensions, numerous top-notch trainers have arrived for showdowns!"/\rPick your challenge - rewards await you!"Y\rYou may also look for me to return your Pokemon to you if you lose your challenge."\rAll the best!"3\rWelcome back! Here's your remaining Pokemon."#\rDon't give up! Do try again!"4Announcer: You're gonna quit now? Are you sure?"!\bAnnouncer: Please head up."\bHey \PN."g\bThis is where you are gonna be partnering up with someone of your choice, to take on other duos."r\bThe combination is endless and up to your decision. This also means victory is not up to your full control."\bExciting right?"Y\bHey, partner! Can I interest you in some moves? They don't have these anywhere else, you know.\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas,Dual Wingbeat, Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam,Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage, Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]" \bCome again! Or not. Hehe."\bAny other moves?\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas, Dual Wingbeat,Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam, Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage,Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]"0\bAnother worthy challenger comes and goes."Y\bI see your excitement and unwavering determination. You should have what it takes."U\bDon't give up, young man! Just like me. I've been here for ages now. Hohohoho."<PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE JUKEBOX MENU..."+WELCOME [\PN]! PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR BGM."\ch[77,-1,Default Beats]"a\ch[77,,Default Beats,Spring Violin,Summer Flute,Autumn Guitar,Winter Harmonica,Night Piano]"M\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep up yourself."L\rHave a break. Grab a cuppa joe. Take a quickie in the loo. Go for it!"C\rOnce you are ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"#\rWhat a bummer. I lost again.">\rIt's really hard to conquer them with just 3 Pokemon..."+\rTEACH ME. HOW DO I WIN AGAINST THEM?"T\bHey \PN, you chose the Gauntlet huh. So what would you like me to talk about?"�\bThis challenge is simple. Basically, it's a survival mode. Keep fighting your challengers till you fall. So don't be disheartened or sad that you lost. You did your very best."l\bBut making it neverending seems like no way out yea? So I kept the limit at 100. Good to know, right?"Z\bOne last tip, check with Nurse Joy from time to time, alright? Now get going! Shoo!"<\bLet me check......\nYour current win count is \v[81]."
\bOne. More. Match.\nAre you shaking in fear? Trembling with excitement? Or you are gonna strut out of this place with your head held high? You've done great nonetheless. :) Screenshot this and look for me in Discord, you are worthy of the role: [Gauntlet Maniac]!!!"�\bUrgh... I am tired of looking at your face now. Just kidding. Look at the time. How long has it been? Have you eaten? Had a bath? You are getting there real soon!"�\bSheesh, you are still here? You must have shown real determination to last till now. You should screenshot this moment and show it off!"�\bYou have passed the halfway mark! Congratulations! So what's this going to be? The end for you? Or you gonna keep going up to this seemingly... endless... cycle...?"s\bHonestly, you did well. This is a good number for dedicated players. Give yourself a pat on your back. Yeah!"Z\bAlright, you got so far! What are you still standing here for? Hmmmm? Taking a nap?"�\bOk, this is decent for casual players. I would like to thank you for challenging Gauntlet and making my efforts worthwhile. :)"�\bYou might be facing some struggles now. Maybe consider grinding more in Practice and Club? Redeem more goodies to boost your Pokemon!"U\bStop checking your win count when you can count them with one hand. Sheesh. :)"^\bStop checking your win count when you don't even need a hand to count it. Sheeeeesh. :)"`\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Let me explain how it works."w\bThe Club Challenge is really just a small taste of what's to come in other parts of the Grandeur Club. Hehehe..."�\bDepending on the difficulty you picked earlier, you will fight a certain amount of trainers. For Rookie, that's 3 Gym Leaders, for Veteran that's 4 Gym Leaders and an Elite 4 member and for Ace that's 5 Gym Leaders, 2 Elite 4 members and a "Champion"."?\bAt the end, talk to Hitsu for a reward for your efforts!"S\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Want some tips?"�\bFirst off, you might want to consider using moves with a slightly lower base power but have more PP than the moves you currently have."y\bThat way, you don't run out of PP for a move and lose type coverage in the middle of a battle, which really sucks."\bSource? Trust me, mate."�\bNext, you should definitely consider giving your Pokémon a good spread of EVs. That way you're not leaving the opponent on 1 HP!"x\bYou might want to also consider using some status moves rather than just brute forcing your way through a battle."%\bThat's all from me, good luck!"&\bBoo. Oh well, good luck anyway."5Announcer: You are gonna quit now? Are you sure?"R\rAfter a tough time, I finally got through one of the Club challenges. Phew."d\rDon't mind me. I am just pondering about what Pokémon I should bring next for my challenges."T\bHi, this is the entrance for the PRACTICE CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"|\bAnd which region will you be challenging? \ch[98,-1,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos, Alola,Galar,Hisui,Frontier]"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Club Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Club Challenge."F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokemon looks really roughed up."Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, i am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"%\rHehe, desperate yea? Alrighty!"7\rAll's great now! Take care! Please come again!!!"H\rHey! You can't afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rAwwww, be careful out there. *wink*"U\bHehe, I keep getting paired up with the Champions! What a joke of a challenge."~\b... is what I would say if that wasn't a dream I had last night. I actually just get Gym Leaders as my choices. AHHHHH!"S\b<i>Sobs</i>. <i>Sobs</i>... My team of Rattatas... obliterated. Waaaaaaaaaa~"�\bNow this challenge, i would say is the MOST COMPLICATED CHALLENGE in the entire Grandeur Club. So listen carefully. Or you could just go and learn by stumbling, falling and tripping yourself up."�\bThis is basically a maze, a labyrinth, a penitentiary. You choose and enter 1 of the 6 entrances, and you gotta escape by collecting 5 keys. Keys will be given out to random trainers, so you know, you gotta defeat them to get the keys."�\bOnce you've gotten all 5 keys, all entrances are now exits, and you just gotta find your way out. Understand everything now? I wish you all the best. :)"{\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Titan Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)"�\bIn this challenge specifically, you also won't be able to inflict your opponents with status conditions, flinch, trap or confuse them!"�\bLastly, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"{\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Titan Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your mons alive!"i\bAlso, they won't be effective here in the Titan Challenge; all opponents are immune to stat drops."!\bFoul: Why hello there pal!"\bAre you lost?"�\bTook the wrong turn looking for the bathroom? Well don't you worry, just follow me and I will take you back to where you're supposed to be."9\bOh who am I kidding. We both know you're not lost."f\bThis is one of the most secure facilities in this dimension; people don't just get "lost" here."t\bYour luck seems to have run out now that I've found you before the other two, see, I'm not as nice as them..."!\bBut then again, I'm bored."\bEhhh, why not."~\bSee, it would be mean if I defeated you now, but wouldn't it be even meaner if I healed you, just to make you wipe out?"+\bLet me show you what I mean by that!"<\bNot too bad, maybe you do have some skills after all."L\bNow scram and make sure I don't catch you sneaking around here again!"d\bBut maybe leave a resume on your way out. We might need someone of your talent in the future."P\bWhat's up, feeling lost? A newcomer would be overwhelmed with this place."J\bLook for Luc, he will tell you what you to expect in Grandeur Club."a\bHow're you doin'? I hope you are not surprised by the trainers' standard in Grandeur Club."|\bLook for Luc from time to time to understand rules and regulations of various challenges. Re-evaluate your team if needed."K\bIf you are stuck, farm and grind. You will get there. MUAHAHAHAHAHA!""\rThis challenge is so weird."U\rI don't know if I'm holding my partner back, or if it's the other way round..."0\r*sighs* I guess it's all up to luck, huh?"'\bDid you complete the challenges?"<\bI see some trainers come out there from time to time."(\bI wonder what Pokémon they used."S\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Titan Challenge!"F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokémon look really roughed up."v\rVermint: Hello \PN, I hope you enjoy your stay here. Try not to think too much about our first encounter, okay?"W\rVermint: Hello \PN, I had foreseen that I would have to introduce myself to you."^\rMy true name is Vera. I created your wardrobe and I am also here to judge your resolve."-\rI hope this isn't a shock to you, \PN."bThe abyss is deep and dark. You shiver as you can feel overwhelming forces enamating from it."JYou almost blacked out. It would be a good idea to stay away from it."J\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep yourself."B\rOnce you're ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"I\bDon't mind me, I'm just mentally preparing myself before going in."J\bI'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime!"FAn ominous Vending Machine stares at you. Best not to go near it."=PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS ENEMY SYGNA BUFFS..."WELCOME [\PN]!"vYou can't seem to get the Vending Machine to work anymore. Maybe it can only be used before starting a challenge?"#The exit seems to be locked..."?\bThis is a great place to level up your Pokemon to Lv100!"A\bHitsukid made this challenge just for that reason in mind!"�\rI heard a rumour that once upon a time, there were no difficulties for this challenge and that trainers would stack on top of Nurse Joy."M\rTerrifying, right? I'm glad that it doesn't happen anymore, if it did."
\bAsh"\bLance"\bBrawly"c\bLuc-ker: Oh, you want to battle me at my full power? Fine, but don't say you weren't warned."G\bLuc: Too easy, huh? I lied - that wasn't actually my full power."�\bMy real master, Yhwach, gifted me with the shift V - The Visionary, turning my imagination into reality! That means I can throw at you whatever I can conjure and I simply haven't had enough to imagine yet."\bUntil next time!"Z\bLuc: Hehe, that's a taste of what's to come soon. Thanks for letting me go all-out!"MIt's a Vending Machine. Is it like all the other ones in the main lobby?"7PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS SYGNA BUFFS..."�YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION. \ch[98,-1,Buff shop,View active buffs,View unlocked buffs,Add buff, Remove active buff,Clear active buffs,Close menu]")YOU HAVE BOUGHT ALL BUFFS AVAILABLE."YOU HAVE NO ACTIVE BUFFS."%YOU HAVE NO MORE UNLOCKED BUFFS."ACTIVE BUFFS CLEARED."gOh dear, looks like you don't have enough Pokémon to battle. Talk to Nurse Joy to get patched up."#\bPsst! Want to know a secret?"i\bI heard that Luc-ker nearly went insane trying to get trainers from Pasio here for this challenge."e\bAnd oh boy did it work out for him. Now we have these monstrosities disguised as "challenges"."H\bThey're not even "challenges", they're just straight up bullying!"�\bI guess the one saving grace is the existence of blessings... an idea he got after playing far too much of a rougue-like mode in a certain game."\bHaha, your loss then."C\rDid you know that there's a way to get to the higher floors?"O\rI hear that only strong trainers or certain VIPs will have access to it."�\rHow do you know if you're strong? I heard another rumour that, if you get good in Club, and I mean <i>real good</i> in Club, they'll acknowledge you."7\rHope you will be one to get there. All the best!"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Duet Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Duet Challenge."G\rHey! You cant afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rHmm... what blessings should I use?"}\rI could use "Assassin's Blessing" for that extra speed so that my Lucario has enough speed to outspeed almost everything..."�\bBut I also need it to hit hard enough, so I want "Warrior's Blessing"... or should I swap to a special set and use "Warlock's Blessing" to power up my Regieleki even further...?"�\rAh, but then I can't get Unflappable to deal with whatever <i>that<\i> is... ugh. Maybe just Lv 2 on one of my blessings then?"^\rHuh? You don't know what I'm talking about? Hahaha, you haven't lost to them, have you?"X\rYou're either really good, or you haven't been whooped yet. Either way, have fun!"5\bOnly authorized staffs are permitted to enter."1\ch[98,-1,Display your Staff Pass,Walk Away]"b\bOh, you are one of the staff here? You should have show me your pass earlier. Please enter."\bPlease leave. Thank you."�\bFoul: Hello! Glad to see that you are finally here. In case you don't recognise me, my name is Foul Play at A Garbodor Price, but my friends call me Foul."�\bI am one of the few people to be chosen here before you to test my strength against this place. And I can tell you from experience that you are gonna have a lot of fun, or not. It depends on you after all."q\bTonnes of huge experimental vessels containing floating specimens in colourful bubbly liquids can be seen."9\bMan, I love this challenge despite how hard it is."w\bThe different trainers you get to face, their unique gimmicks, their drip and even the blessings you get to use."\bIt's beautiful. :')"P\bHi, this is the entrance for the CLUB CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"K\bHi, this is the entry for MAYHEM CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your original bag back soon enough.">\bYou have a Backstage Pass. Let me tear that up for you."R\bHow strange. You don't seem to have a backstage pass. Try buying one again." \bPlease let me escort you."�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your bag back soon enough."1\bIntriguing coloured-specimens can be seen."7\bOut of bou...... hmmmm? Let me answer this call.",\bYes sir? Yes. Yes. He is here. Roger."N\bApologies. You may enter and access the higher floor as of now. Please."8\bHope you're having fun in the Grandeur Club, \PN!"/\bWant to refresh yourself on a challenge?"T\bYo! I'm Luc-ker, nice to meet you, \PN! (The hyphen is important by the way.)"�\bHmm? How do I know your name? Ahahaha, don't worry about the specifics. By the way, you can call me Luc for short if my full name is too hard for you."o\bAnyway, I'm here to help you out by giving you some information on the challenges, as Hitsu wants me to."X\bYou'd better jot them down on a piece of paper, instead of just spamming confirm!"i\bThere's 6 main challenges to take on in the Grandeur Club. Which one would you like to know about?"~\ch[1,-1,Club Challenge, Practice Challenge, Gauntlet Challenge, Mayhem Challenge,Sync Challenge, Titan Challenge,Finish]"W\bThe Club Challenge - here, you can battle characters from the main series games."\bIf you can battle characters from the anime and Pokémon Adventures, then why not the same for the main series games as well?"w\bYou'll be facing Lv 90 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle. If you do well enough, you might get some... *ahem* privileges.",\bAnything else you would like to know?"b\bThe Practice Challenge. If the Club Challenge is too difficult for you, try this challenge!"\bSimilar to Club Challenge, but the Pokémon are at Lv 75 and hold no items, so it's a good place to grind your Pokémon!"}\bThe Gauntlet Challenge, the challenge that chucks trainers at you until your team drops (or until you defeat 150 trainers)."{\bYou will be facing Lv 100 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle, with benefits at certain intervals to help you build your win streak."�\bYour longest, most glorious run will be logged for you so you can boast in Discord with fellow players, so whip out the big guns!"x\bThe Mayhem Challenge - in this one, you battle with trainers in a full battles and they have all Lv 100 Pokémon."�\bIf you pay attention, you'll realise that even if you face the same trainer on next run, their team line-up is hardly the same!"~\bThat's because they're holding a pool of Pokémon awaiting for your arrival. You'll never know what's up their sleeves!"^\bThey have high IVs as well, so you'd better bring your best 6, because THIS IS MADNESS!"�\bThe Sync Challenge; you'll battle "Sygna Suit" trainers (and other outfits) from the hit mobile game "Pokémon Masters EX" in 3v3 triple battles."�\bTheir Pokémon may also have special gimmicks, for example not needing to recharge after using a move with high base power, or not being able to miss attacks."B\bYou'd better bring your lucky charm, the challenge is real!"�\bThe Titan challenge you'll be battling Sync Pokémon, also known as Titans, in a 6v1 triple battle. <s>This was made before Scarlet and Violet, way before they thought it was cool.</s>"}\bThey'll be retaining their gimmick from the Sync Challenge, but they're much tankier, and you can't rely on AOE moves."}\bHitsu's idea is this is to mimic the scenario of Quest Raids from certain RPG games. So ready up, and go for the head!"2\bPhew! Thanks for that. Good luck out there!"\bWhat the heck."q\bI took my Necrozma to the Hyper Trainer to max out its IVs. It has 252 EVs in Special Attack. It's Modest."j\bSO WHY THE HECK, AFTER ULTRA BURSTING, IS ITS Z-MOVE ONLY HITTING FOR 30-35% ON MISTY'S POKÉMON???"\bARGHHHHHH!"\bShow me your best!"O\bBrock: The world is huge. There are still many strong trainers like you."0\bI have faith that you will overcome them!"C\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your team looks really roughed up."{\rThe unit behind me broke down, so that's no more healing for you for the rest of the challenge, for better or worse."!\rCome back again next time!"B\rThe unit is all charged up. Let's heal your team, shall we?"3\rAll's great now! Put your best foot out, ok?"g\rHehe, desperate yea? I could heal you up with the unit behind me, but it is still not ready yet."|YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION.\ch[98,-1,View active buffs,Other options?,Close menu]"iThe other options have been grayed out. Maybe they can only be accessed before starting a challenge?"\rSheeeeeeeesh."}\rEither these Titans have a ridiculous amount of health and/or defenses, or our damage is being reduced by an insane amount."N\rWelp. Either way, it sure feels like I'm facing a JRPG boss every time."<\bCongrats, you made it through the PRACTICE CHALLENGE!"@\bDepending on the difficulty selected, here's your reward."+\b1 GC Credit has been awarded to you.")\bDo compete again for more rewards!"c\bYou may exit by following the arrow sign; it's best not to loiter around this area. Alright?"?\bNo no no. No more rewards. But you can always try again?"8\bCongrats, you made it through the CLUB CHALLENGE!"-\b2 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b5 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b3 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b10 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b20 GC Credits have been awarded to you."<\bCongrats, you made it through the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE!"1\bDepending on your run, here's your reward.":\bCongrats, you made it through the MAYHEM CHALLENGE!".\b25 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b50 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b75 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the DUET CHALLENGE!".\b15 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b40 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the SYNC CHALLENGE!"2\b\v[61] GC Credits have been awarded to you."9\bCongrats, you made it through the TITAN CHALLENGE!"\\rHeh. No matter how many times you do this challenge, there are no two identical runs."c\rWell, ok. Maybe there is, but it's like a 0.000000000000000000000000000000000000001% chance."�\bLike, seriously. There are so many trainers and their teams might not even be the same each time, even if you face the same trainer."u\rAND it might not even be in the same order or rooms as in the previous run, even if the trainers are the same."=\bAh, the challenges here are way tougher than expected.""\bI am kinda bummed about it."(\bHow about you? Are you up for it?".\bHow's it going? Bet you're doing great!"B\bYou will overcome and make your way back here again. Right?"B\bHmm. It's so hard to formulate a strategy for each trainer."�\bThing is, there's no such thing as a "perfect lead". You could lead off with a Ferrothorn and it would do amazing against Marlon, but then it would get one shot from any of Flint's Pokémon."o\bAnd then you'd have to waste items... or even worse, have one less Pokémon for the rest of the battles."9\rWow, this is delicious! One more on the go please!"e\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you are taking this chance to grind your Pokemon up to tip-top!"E\r..........hope you are not coming here for a quick heal, yeah?"_\rWow... Erm, this service is not available in the Practice Challenge. Apologies for that."$\rDo your very best... alright?"8\rNurse Joy: Great! You go and get those wins, \PN!"/\bThis is inhumane. I might call it a day."*\bI was fired from my job last month."�\bNow I have nothing better to do than grind this. My longest win streak is 70... healing is a lot less frequent the higher you go."]\bHi, this is the entrance for the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE. Your highest win count is \v[93]."\bWould you like to enter?">\bThis curry dish is just like my challenges in the Club."\bKICKIN' my ass... Sobs."9\bBwahahahaha. I... am having shivers on this floor.";PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE REWARD MENU..."aWELCOME [\PN]! YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR REWARD TO REDEEM."�\ch[98,-1,***SPECIAL OFFER DEAL***, Enhancements (1 Credit),Alterfication (3 Credits), Lounge BGM Pack (10 Credits),Gems (1 Credit), Held Items,Credit-Money Exchange]"o\ch[75,-1, Code: Luck (2 Credits), VIP Backstage Pass (5 Credits), Grandeur Club Staff Pass (500 Credits)]"(PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!">YOU HAVE INSUFFICIENT CREDIT. PLEASE COME BACK NEXT TIME.""REDEEM SUCCESSFUL! THANK YOU!"0BACKSTAGE PASS NOT FOR SALE YET! THANK YOU!".BACKSTAGE PASS ALREADY BOUGHT! THANK YOU!"7YOU ALREADY OWN A STAFF PASS. COME BACK NEXT TIME."c\ch[75,-1,Intensity Tonic, Vigor Serum, Dense Extract,Hidden Stimulant,Apex Vaccine,Bolt Brew]"U\ch[75,-1,Code: Breath,Code: Grim,Code: Wall,Code: Storm,Code: Dome,Code: Shine]"WLOUNGE BGM PACK ALREADY BOUGHT AND DOWNLOADED! PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!"=LOUNGE BGM PACK DOWNLOADED INTO GRANDEUR PAD! THANK YOU!"L\ch[98,-1,1 Credit,2 Credits,3 Credits,5 Credits,8 Credits,10 Credits ]"d\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challenge. Let me explain how it works."�\bThe Practice Challenge is essentially an easier version of the Club Challenge so that you can level up your Pokémon in preparation for it. In other words, we designed this challenge for grinding."V\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challnge. Want some tips?"Z\bSorry, you need at least 3 Pokémon that are able to battle for the Sync challenge."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the SYNC CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"S\bPlease do not disturb me. I need to formulate a strategy for the challenges."APLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS YOUR GRANDEUR RECORDS..."CWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club]"$Your Practice Records is empty." Your Club Records is empty."XWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club,Gauntlet,Duet,Mayhem]"$Your Gauntlet Records is empty." Your Duet Records is empty.""Your Mayhem Records is empty."T\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Mayhem Challenge!"Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, I am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"O\rI heard there are many more challengers from around the world have here."I\rThis will allow me to know where I stand in my journey to the top!"Yes"No"Rookie"Veteran"Ace"Master"Challenge"Win Counts"Cancel"Backstage"	Yes?"No![�"G\bMe duele la cabeza de pensar en cómo superar estos desafíos..."`\b¿Necesito movimientos de mucho daño? ¿O debería debilitarlos con tácticas y estados?"m\bO quizá deba mejorar los EV de mis Pokémon... o peor aún, ponerme a buscar Pokémon con IV altos..."H\bHola, esta es la entrada al DESAFÍO DÚO. ¿Te gustaría entrar?"/\b¿Y en qué dificultad vas a participar?"\bClaro."*\rEnfermera Joy: ¡Buenos días, \PN!"0\r¿Te gustaría recibir algo de curación?"\r... ¡y listo! ¡Ta-da!"�\rNo puedo creer que me hayas hecho restaurar por completo a tu equipo, desgraciado. Esto ni siquiera se suponía que existiera."l\r¿Cómo? ¿Esperabas una curación completa? Ja, ja, no seas ridículo. Esto ya es bastante generoso.";\rTu equipo ya debería estar con toda la salud, ¿no?"6\r¡Espero que lo pases bien en el Desafío Sync!"-\bElige tu entrada. \ch[73,,A,B,C,D,E,F]"5\bHumph, si esto fuera una pelea a puñetazos..."J\bHola, esta es la entrada al DESAFÍO TITÁN. ¿Te gustaría entrar?"�\bLuc-ker: ¡Ey, \PN! ¿Has venido a enfrentarte al Desafío Sync? Estoy deseando ver tu reacción ante los Entrenadores de aquí, jeje. ;)"2\bLuc-ker: ¿Quieres algunos consejos? Claro."�\bAquí hay bastantes Entrenadores, así que vamos a dividirlos por regiones.\ch[98,-1,Consejos generales,Términos clave,Kanto, Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Aniversario, Neo Campeón,Mejoras Sygna]"�\bAquí hay bastantes Entrenadores, así que vamos a dividirlos por regiones.\ch[98,-1,Consejos generales,Términos clave,Kanto,Johto, Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Aniversario,Neo Campeón]"(\bBuena suerte, la vas a necesitar."�\bY no te preocupes si pierdes, ¡seguirás recibiendo Créditos GC por intentarlo! Eso sí, siempre que no pulses F12 porque seas mal perdedor o demasiado tryhard."�\b¿Quieres algunos consejos generales? Hmm. El mejor consejo que puedo darte aquí es que esperes lo inesperado. No juegan con el meta de la saga principal, juegan con el meta de PoMas."�\bPor ejemplo, se subirán las estadísticas mucho más de lo que deberían, inventarán mecánicas nuevas, ignorarán Protección y se curarán más de la cuenta, por decir solo algunas cosas."�\bTambién tendrán movimientos interesantes, desde movimientos usados por sus Entrenadores en lugar de por el Pokémon hasta movimientos poderosos que solo pueden usarse bajo ciertas condiciones."�\bAdemás, movimientos cheese como Mismo Destino y Canto Mortal no funcionarán aquí; Desarme tampoco les quitará sus objetos. ¡Ni lo intentes!"�\bPero por último, y quizá aquí veas una parte positiva: he hecho que no solo te beneficies de una cierta reducción de daño, sino que además los Entrenadores "más duros" tengan menos probabilidades de aparecer pronto."�\bAsí que, si quieres familiarizarte con los Entrenadores de aquí, quizá sea buena idea probar primero este desafío en una dificultad más baja.";\bEn cualquier caso, buena suerte, la vas a necesitar."�\bClaro. ¿Cuál quieres que te explique? \ch[1,-1,Ratio de crítico,Movimiento de Entrenador,Movimiento B,Habilidad pasiva,Pasiva Máster,Zona,Curación gradual]"v\bRatio de crítico: la frecuencia con la que un Pokémon asesta golpes críticos, hasta un máximo de 3 niveles."�\bMovimiento de Entrenador: un movimiento que usa el Entrenador (en lugar de su Pokémon). Estos movimientos suelen potenciar al Pokémon del usuario o al lado de su equipo."h\bPueden usarse incluso cuando el Pokémon del Entrenador está afectado por un problema de estado."�\bMovimiento B: significa Buddy Move. Puedes identificarlos por el "descriptor" en el nombre del movimiento, por ejemplo: Placaje Eléctrico Origen."�\bSuelen hacer lo mismo que el movimiento en el que se basan, pero con más potencia, efectos añadidos o una mejora del efecto habitual."�\bNormalmente hay una condición que debe cumplirse antes de poder usar cada Movimiento B, así que aprovéchalo para contrarrestarlos."�\bSi no la tienen, seguramente será porque tendrán muy pocos PP. Por último, todos los Entrenadores tienen como máximo 1 Movimiento B, aunque hay 1 excepción."qHabilidad pasiva: básicamente una habilidad extra, pero no puede ser ignorada por efectos como Rompemoldes."�\bLa cantidad de estas que tiene un Pokémon es totalmente arbitraria, aunque he intentado limitarla a un máximo de 3, sin contar las Pasivas Máster."t\bPasiva Máster: una Habilidad Pasiva que aumenta el daño infligido por el equipo y reduce el daño recibido."\bHay 3 tipos: Portaestandarte sirve para todos los movimientos y otorga un 10% más de daño y un 20% menos de daño recibido."s\bOrgullo se aplica a los movimientos físicos y otorga un 20% más de daño y un 25% menos de daño recibido."\bPor último, Espíritu se aplica a los movimientos especiales y otorga un 20% más de daño y un 25% menos de daño recibido."z\bZona: un efecto de campo como el clima o el terreno, que potencia en un 50% los movimientos de un determinado tipo."{\bCuración gradual: el Pokémon recupera 1/16 de sus PS máximos en cada turno. Piensa en ello como si fueran Restos."Y\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,Brock,Misty,Erika, Red,Red (Thunderbolt),Blue,Leaf]"o\bProbablemente Brock tenga el kit más básico de todos aquí, ya que fue el primer Traje Sygna de PoMas."�\bEn cualquier caso, su Movimiento de Entrenador da +1 Defensa a Tyranitar y hace que su siguiente ataque acierte seguro y sea crítico, pero hay formas de evitarlo, como Protección."�\bTtar tiene 2 pasivas. Una hace que sus movimientos tengan más probabilidades de aplicar sus efectos adicionales y la otra evita que le bajen las estadísticas bajo tormenta de arena."�\bMisty también tiene un kit muy básico. Su Movimiento de Entrenador da +2 Defensa a su Vaporeon y +2 Defensa Especial a su lado del campo."�\bPor último, las pasivas de su Vaporeon le dan curación gradual al entrar en combate, además de una probabilidad de subir su Evasión tras usar un movimiento."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Erika da +2 Ataque y +1 ratio de crítico a su Leafeon, pero si hay sol, esas subidas se duplican."V\bLa habilidad de Leafeon es Clorofila, así que con sol su Velocidad se duplica."l\bAdemás, sus pasivas impiden que sufra problemas de estado y lo curan después de usar un movimiento."K\bEn otras palabras: ¡de verdad no quieres ver a Leafeon bajo el sol!"�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Red da +3 Ataque, At. Esp. y Velocidad a su Charizard, además de +2 ratio de crítico, aunque le baja en -1 la Defensa y la Defensa Especial."�\bSu Charizard también tiene pasivas que hacen que sus movimientos nunca fallen y que no necesiten un turno de recarga tras usarlos."q\b¿Sabes lo que significa eso? Puede usar Sofoco. Todos. Y. Cada. Uno. De. Los. Turnos. ¡Que te diviertas!"�\bEn realidad, Red tiene un segundo Traje Sygna en PoMas. Su Movimiento de Entrenador da +6 Ataque y Curación gradual a Pikachu."�\bPikachu también puede Gigamaxizarse, aunque aquí se aprovecha menos que en PoMas, ya que allí solo se usa 1 movimiento Dinamax por cada pareja compi en cada combate."|\bTambién tiene una Pasiva Máster Portaestandarte. Consulta la sección de Términos clave para saber qué significa."�\bSus otras pasivas hacen que todos sus movimientos sean críticos, además de curarlo después de usar un movimiento en Campo Eléctrico."�\bY por último, aunque no menos importante, Pikachu tiene un Movimiento B que solo puede usarse cuando el Campo Eléctrico está activo."^\bSi tu Pokémon está paralizado, su Defensa y su Defensa Especial también bajan en -1."{\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Blue da +2 Defensa y +1 ratio de crítico a su lado, además de colocar Viento Afín."�\bEn cualquier caso, su Blastoise es un muro de los buenos. Cuando recibe un golpe, una de sus pasivas da +1 Ataque y +1 At. Esp. a su lado."�\bY cuando ataca, su otra pasiva da +1 Defensa Especial a su lado. Por último, tampoco necesita recargarse tras usar Hidrocañón."|\bCon el Movimiento de Entrenador de Leaf me tomé algunas libertades creativas para que estuviera a la altura de su nombre."o\bDa Curación gradual a los Pokémon de su lado, ¡además de curarlos a todos un 40% de sus PS máximos!"�\bEn cuanto a las pasivas de Venusaur, envenenan gravemente a tus Pokémon y les bajan en -1 sus estadísticas defensivas después de ser golpeados por él."m\bCon Hoja Afilada y una Planta Feroz sin recarga, está claro que repartirá muchísimo veneno y daño."^\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,Morty,Ethan,Lyra,Kris, Silver,Giovanni,Giovanni (Ultra)]"�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Morty da +1 Defensa, Defensa Especial y ratio de crítico a su lado, además de colocar Viento Afín."�\bUna de las pasivas de Ho-Oh da aumentos extra de estadísticas a su equipo si usa con éxito un movimiento de estado la primera vez que lo usa en combate."a\bSu otra pasiva cura a los Pokémon del lado de Ho-Oh cuando usa un movimiento bajo el sol."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Ethan potencia el siguiente movimiento especial de Lugia, le da +1 Precisión y hace que su siguiente movimiento sea crítico."�\bLugia tiene pasivas que hacen que sus ataques de objetivo único golpeen a todos los rivales, además de restaurar PP al Movimiento de Entrenador de Ethan."~\bPor último, también tiene una Pasiva Máster Espíritu. Consulta la sección de Términos clave para saber qué significa."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Lyra da +2 Ataque y +2 At. Esp. a un Pokémon de su lado, además de darle Curación gradual. Pero eso no es lo más loco de esta pareja compi."�\bCelebi tiene pasivas que dejan al rival retrocediendo, atrapado y confundido después de usar un movimiento, y además bajan una de las estadísticas del objetivo en -2."�\bYyyyy además Celebi tiene Fitoimpulso y puede colocar también Campo de Hierba para darle prioridad. ¡Menuda combinación asquerosa!"|\bPor último, también tiene una Pasiva Máster Orgullo. Consulta la sección de Términos clave para saber qué significa."]\bSi te enfrentas a ella, reza para que las otras parejas compi sean atacantes físicos."\\bDe base, su Movimiento de Entrenador da +2 At. Esp. y +1 ratio de crítico a su lado."�\bPero si está lloviendo, también potencia el siguiente ataque especial de su equipo, haciendo que peguen todavía más fuerte."�\bUna de las pasivas de Suicune da +4 Defensa Especial a su lado si usa con éxito un movimiento de estado la primera vez que lo usa en combate."�\bSu otra pasiva cura a su equipo después de usar un movimiento bajo la lluvia. Creo que ya te haces una idea: ¡la lluvia es peligrosa si te enfrentas a Kris!"{\bPor último, tiene una Pasiva Máster Portaestandarte. Consulta la sección de Términos clave para saber qué significa."|\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Silver da +3 Ataque y Velocidad a Sneasel, además de colocar Viento Afín en su lado."�\bEl Movimiento B de Sneasel, Triple Axel Demoledor, solo puede usarse cuando sus PS están al máximo. En teoría, eso no parece muy difícil de contrarrestar, ¿no?"�\bPues bien, en cada golpe de un movimiento múltiple, sus pasivas bajan en -1 la Velocidad del Pokémon rival mientras él gana +1 Evasión."�\bAdemás, gana +1 ratio de crítico con cada golpe de su Movimiento B, aunque no tiene muchas otras formas de aumentar su daño por sí mismo."|\bAsí que, en el mejor de los casos, tienes suerte y lo debilitas de un solo golpe; en el peor, es una auténtica molestia."J\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Giovanni da +6 Ataque a su Nidoking."x\bSu Nidoking tiene una pasiva que hace que todos sus ataques sean golpes críticos, incluidos sus movimientos Max."�\bSu otra pasiva convierte los movimientos de tipo Normal en movimientos de tipo Tierra, permitiéndole beneficiarse del STAB. ¡Su Megapatada va a doler bastante!"�\bEsta versión de Giovanni tiene un Movimiento de Entrenador que da +2 Ataque y At. Esp. a su lado, además de hacer que Guzzlord se convierta en el centro de atención."�\bGuzzlord tiene pasivas que permiten que las subidas de Defensa y Defensa Especial de Reserva se tripliquen y se compartan con sus aliados."]\bSin embargo, como consecuencia de esto, solo puede usar Reserva un máximo de 2 veces."�\bAdemás, Guzzlord no tiene solo 1 Movimiento B, ¡sino 2! Es la única excepción a la "regla" que dice que solo puede haber 1 Movimiento B por pareja compi."�\bCuando se usan, ambos eliminan las subidas de estadísticas de Reserva y restauran 1 PP al Movimiento de Entrenador de Giovanni."�\bEl primero, Trago Devorador, solo puede usarse después de haber usado Reserva y restaura los PS de Guzzlord en función de cuántas veces se haya usado."@\bDespués, restaura una cantidad fija de PS a sus aliados."|\bEl segundo es Triturar Voraz. Solo puede usarse cuando las subidas de Defensa y Defensa Especial de Guzzlord son 6 o más."B\bLuego baja en -1 las estadísticas defensivas del objetivo."?\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,May,Brendan,Steven,Wally]"�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de May da +4 Ataque y +1 Precisión a su Blaziken, coloca Viento Afín y lo protege del daño durante el resto del turno."�\bLa primera pasiva de Blaziken da +1 Velocidad a su lado al entrar en combate, incluida su Megaevolución, lo que en la práctica se traduce en un aumento de +2."�\bSu otra pasiva baja en -2 la Defensa del objetivo. En resumen, es rapidísimo y puede descontrolarse con facilidad si no tienes cuidado."{\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Brendan da +4 At. Esp. y Defensa Especial a su lado, además de +1 ratio de crítico."�\bLa primera pasiva de su Latios potencia los siguientes movimientos especiales de su lado al entrar en combate y al Megaevolucionar."�\bSu otra pasiva aumenta la probabilidad de efectos adicionales; si se trata de una bajada de estadísticas, también se duplicará."i\bTiene Resplandor, así que eso significa que recibirás mucho daño especial si no tienes cuidado."�\bSteven... es mucho. Como tiene un Deoxys, PoMas decidió darle no solo 1 forma de Deoxys, ¡sino las 4! Así que vamos a desglosarlo un poco.\ch[2,-1,Estado inicial,Rasgos compartidos,Forma Normal,Forma Ataque,Forma Defensa,Forma Velocidad]"�\bAl principio, Deoxys empieza en su Forma Normal con 4 Movimientos de Entrenador y una pasiva que le da +1 Precisión al entrar."�\bEl primero, "¡Prueba esto!", coloca Campo Psíquico y da +2 Defensa, At. Esp., Def. Esp. y Velocidad a Deoxys, manteniéndolo en su Forma Normal."s\bEl segundo, "¡Ataca!", da +6 At. Esp. y +3 ratio de crítico a Deoxys, y luego lo cambia a su Forma Ataque."�\bEl tercero, "¡Defiende!", da +4 Ataque y At. Esp. a su lado. Después, Deoxys cambia a su Forma Defensa y se protege del daño durante el resto del turno."�\bPor último, aunque no menos importante, "¡Más rápido!" da +6 Velocidad y +3 Evasión a Deoxys y lo cambia a su Forma Velocidad."�\bFuera de su estado inicial, todas las formas de Deoxys que usa Steven tienen una pasiva que convierte las bajadas de estadísticas en subidas, ¡pero no al revés como hace Respondón!"k\bTodas tienen también Psicoataque y Cabezazo Zen, así que no volveré a mencionarlos más adelante."j\bEn su Forma Normal, Deoxys tiene Recuperación y Poder Cósmico además de los movimientos comunes."�\bTambién tiene una pasiva que aumenta la probabilidad de efectos adicionales, así que si usa Cabezazo Zen, ¡prepárate para retroceder!"h\bEn su Forma Ataque, Deoxys tiene Protección y Poder Cósmico además de los movimientos comunes."�\bTambién tiene una pasiva que aumenta la potencia de sus siguientes movimientos físicos y especiales, así que podría descontrolarse muy rápido."l\bEn su Forma Defensa, Deoxys tiene Recuperación y Defensa Férrea además de los movimientos comunes."�\bTambién tiene una pasiva que da +2 Defensa Especial a su lado cada vez que se usa un movimiento de estado, así que con Defensa Férrea se volverá muy resistente enseguida."k\bEn su Forma Velocidad, Deoxys tiene Recuperación y Doble Equipo además de los movimientos comunes."�\bTambién tiene una pasiva que coloca Viento Afín para su lado cuando un movimiento de estado tiene éxito la primera vez que se usa en combate."t\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Wally da +2 At. Esp. y +1 Defensa Especial y ratio de crítico a su Gardevoir."�\bGardevoir tiene 2 pasivas: la primera da +1 Velocidad a su lado al entrar en combate y al Megaevolucionar; la otra deja confundido al objetivo después de usar un movimiento."�\bGardevoir también tiene un Movimiento B, Brillo Mágico Supremo. Baja en -4 el Ataque y el At. Esp. de los objetivos, y luego los vuelve más débiles a los ataques de tipo Hada."�\bSolo puede usarse una vez, pero no puedes protegerte de él con Protección, y un -4 en tus estadísticas ofensivas seguramente te obligará a cambiar de Pokémon."[\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,Cynthia,Cynthia (Renegade),Cynthia (Aura),Cyrus,Dawn]"�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Cynthia, con el que me tomé algunas libertades creativas, aumenta el ratio de crítico de su Kommo-o y potencia su siguiente ataque especial según lo bajos que estén sus PS."�\bAparte de eso, Kommo-o tiene pasivas que le permiten ignorar la reducción de daño de Reflejo, Pantalla Luz y Velo Aurora, además de aumentar la probabilidad de efectos adicionales."�\bEsta versión del Movimiento de Entrenador de Cynthia da +4 Ataque y At. Esp., además de +3 ratio de crítico a Giratina. También puede colocar una Zona Fantasma."\\bLos ataques de su Giratina bajan en -1 la Defensa y la Defensa Especial del objetivo."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de esta Cynthia da +4 Defensa y Defensa Especial a su lado, pero si hay una Zona Lucha activa, dará +6 en su lugar."q\bY como su Lucario tiene una pasiva que coloca una Zona Lucha al entrar, la mayoría de las veces será +6."~\bLa otra pasiva de Lucario también depende de la Zona Lucha: si está activa, cura a su lado después de usar un movimiento."�\bTambién tiene Esfera Aural Superior, un Movimiento B que nunca falla y solo puede usarse después de que Lucario haya sido atacado dos veces."a\bDespués de hacer daño, potencia los siguientes ataques físicos y especiales de su lado."�\bPor último, Lucario tiene una Pasiva Máster Portaestandarte. Consulta la sección de Términos clave para saber qué significa."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Cyrus da +2 At. Esp., +1 Precisión y +1 ratio de crítico a su Darkrai. Además, puede colocar una Zona Oscura."�\bDarkrai tiene pasivas que potencian sus movimientos si el objetivo está dormido, o si usa un movimiento de estado, bajará en -1 una estadística aleatoria de todos los rivales."\\bTiene Brecha Negra, pero incluso si falla, su segunda pasiva se activará igualmente."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Dawn da +2 Defensa, Defensa Especial y ratio de crítico a su lado, pero su Cresselia recibe daño de retroceso equivalente al 30% de sus PS restantes."�\bQuizá estés pensando: ¿por qué hacer eso, cuando la mayoría de los otros Movimientos de Entrenador no tienen inconvenientes?"z\bCresselia ya es muy resistente, pero una de sus pasivas la vuelve aún más dura cuando tiene un 50% de PS o menos."�\bSu otra pasiva también aumenta la potencia de los movimientos especiales de su lado si Cresselia usa un movimiento de estado cuando tiene un 50% de PS o menos."]\bTambién tiene Luz Lunar para curarse, ¡así que no cantes victoria demasiado pronto!"W\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,Elesa,Grimsley,Hilbert,Hilda,N, Roxie,Ingo,Emmet]"�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Elesa da +2 Precisión y +2 ratio de crítico a un Pokémon de su lado, además de dar +2 At. Esp. a todos los Pokémon de su lado."{\bRotom tiene una pasiva que le da +1 Evasión cuando recibe un golpe, además de otra que impide que le bajen la Evasión."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Grimsley hace que su Sharpedo reciba daño de retroceso equivalente al 90% de sus PS restantes, pero a cambio le da +6 Ataque, +6 Evasión y +3 ratio de crítico."�\bAdemás, tiene pasivas que aumentan la probabilidad de los efectos adicionales de sus movimientos y aumentan su potencia cuando Sharpedo está en apuros."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Hilbert da +3 At. Esp., +2 ratio de crítico y potencia el siguiente ataque especial de su Genesect."�\bAl usar Tecno Shock, Genesect cambia de forma según el tipo al que el objetivo sea más débil. Además, su tipo por defecto es Bicho en lugar de Normal."i\bDespués, vuelve al objetivo más débil a ese tipo y aplica un efecto correspondiente a ese tipo."�\bEléctrico - Paraliza al objetivo.\n Fuego - Baja en -1 el Ataque del objetivo.\n Hielo - 50% de probabilidad de congelar al objetivo."O\bAgua - Baja en -1 la Defensa del objetivo. Bicho - Sin efecto adicional."l\bPor último, si Genesect asesta un golpe supereficaz, su pasiva baja en -2 la Velocidad del objetivo."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Hilda aumenta el At. Esp. de su Victini en la misma cantidad en la que haya subido su Ataque, luego le da +3 ratio de crítico y +1 Precisión a su equipo."�\bEsto se complementa con las pasivas de Victini, que le dan +2 Ataque al entrar y convierten las bajadas de estadísticas en subidas."�\bY todavía hay más sinergia: Victini tiene V de Fuego, así que se vuelve más resistente y más rápido cada vez que lo usa."X\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de N da +4 Ataque y +3 ratio de crítico a su Kyurem."�\bCuando Kyurem se carga para usar Impactrueno, tiene una pasiva que reduce a la mitad el daño que recibe mientras se carga y desbloquea su Movimiento B, Rugido Noble Resonante."~\bBaja en -2 el Ataque, At. Esp. y Velocidad de todos los Pokémon rivales, a la vez que potencia su siguiente ataque físico."�\bDespués, Impactrueno debe volver a cargarse antes de poder usarse otra vez, lo que evita que se pueda spammear sin parar (además, solo tiene 3 PP)."�\bKyurem también tiene una pasiva que le permite ignorar los efectos de aguante del rival, aunque imagino que eso no saldrá muy a menudo."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Roxie da +4 At. Esp. y +3 ratio de crítico a su Toxtricity, además de aplicar Viento Afín en su lado."Z\bToxtricity tiene 2 pasivas. Una coloca Zona Veneno al entrar y además la prolonga."p\bLa otra baja el Ataque o el At. Esp. del objetivo si este está envenenado o paralizado, respectivamente."|\bAdemás, tiene un Movimiento B, Onda Tóxica Frenética. Solo puede usarse si hay un rival con un problema de estado."�\bNo puede bloquearse con Protección, baja en -2 la Defensa Especial del objetivo y lo envenena si aún no tiene un problema de estado."v\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Ingo da +4 Velocidad y +2 Evasión a su lado. Su Chandelure puede Dinamaxizarse."�\bDespués de usar un movimiento, sus pasivas le dan +2 At. Esp. y +1 ratio de crítico, además de aumentar la potencia de los siguientes movimientos especiales de su equipo."�\bTambién tiene un Movimiento B, Infortunio en Llamas Ascendentes. Solo puede usarse si hay un rival con un problema de estado, o si está retrocediendo, atrapado o confundido."�\bAplica efectos según aquello que tenga el objetivo:\nParálisis - Baja en -2 la Defensa del objetivo.\n Quemadura - Baja en -2 la Defensa Especial del objetivo."v\bVeneno - Se cura un poco de PS a sí mismo y a sus aliados.\n Retroceso - Baja en -2 la Velocidad del objetivo."�\bTrampa - Potencia el siguiente movimiento físico del usuario.\n Confusión - Potencia el siguiente movimiento especial del usuario."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Emmet da inmunidad a Tierra durante 5 turnos a un Pokémon de su lado y hace que sus siguientes movimientos sean críticos. Su Eelektross puede Dinamaxizarse."{\bDespués de usar un movimiento, sus pasivas le dan +2 Ataque y +1 ratio de crítico, además de atrapar al objetivo."�\bTambién tiene un Movimiento B, Voltio Cruel de Rayo Descendente. Solo puede usarse si hay un rival con un problema de estado, o si está retrocediendo, atrapado o confundido."F\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Korrina,Diantha,Lysandre]"v\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Serena da +6 Ataque y At. Esp. a su Zygarde, además de darle Curación gradual."^\bLas pasivas de Zygarde impiden que le bajen las estadísticas y que sus ataques fallen."�\bPor último, también tiene una Pasiva Máster Portaestandarte. Consulta la sección de Términos clave para saber qué significa."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Korrina da +4 Ataque y +3 Velocidad y Evasión a su Marshadow. Después de atacar, la pasiva de Marshadow sube una de sus estadísticas en +1, hasta 3 veces."�\bSi la Defensa de su Diancie ha subido, el Movimiento de Entrenador de Diantha sube su Defensa Especial el mismo número de niveles."g\bDespués, da Curación gradual a Diancie y hace que su siguiente ataque físico haga más daño."�\bEl Movimiento B de Diancie, Tormenta Diamante Rosa, solo puede usarse cuando hay una Zona Roca activa, algo que Diantha puede colocar."K\bBaja en -2 la Defensa del objetivo mientras da +2 Defensa a su lado."�\bLas pasivas de Diancie bajan en -1 la Velocidad de todos los rivales al entrar en combate y al Megaevolucionar, además de darle +2 Ataque y +1 ratio de crítico después de usar un movimiento."s\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Lysandre da +4 At. Esp., +1 Precisión y +3 ratio de crítico a su Volcanion."�\bVolcanion tiene una pasiva que quema a los objetivos a los que golpea. Esto se complementa con su Movimiento B, Hidrobomba Ardiente."�\bSolo puede usarse cuando al menos un Pokémon rival está quemado, y es un movimiento en área que hace más daño a los objetivos quemados."~\bLuego, según a cuántos objetivos quemados golpee, hace que el siguiente ataque especial de Volcanion haga más daño."N\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,Lusamine,Hau,Lana, Acerola,Mina,Gladion]"�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Lusamine da +6 At. Esp. y -1 Velocidad a Necrozma. Su Necrozma Alas del Alba también puede usar Ultraexplosión."�\bTambién tiene pasivas que convierten sus movimientos de objetivo único en movimientos en área y permiten usar Láser Prisma sin que el usuario tenga que recargarse."_\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Hau da +4 At. Esp. y +2 ratio de crítico a su Tapu Koko."\bAl entrar en combate, una de las pasivas de Koko prolonga la duración del Campo Eléctrico que coloca con su habilidad."�\bEsto combina con su otra pasiva, que potencia los siguientes ataques especiales de su lado cuando se aplica un nuevo clima, terreno o zona."}\bDespués, el Movimiento B de Koko, Electrotela Salvaje, puede usarse siempre que haya un clima, terreno o zona activa."�\bDuplica su potencia cuando hay una Zona Hada activa (algo que Hau puede colocar) y baja en -2 la Velocidad de todos los objetivos mientras da +2 Velocidad a Koko y a sus aliados."R\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Lana da +6 Ataque y At. Esp. a su Tapu Lele."~\bAl entrar en combate, una de las pasivas de Lele prolonga la duración del Campo Psíquico que coloca con su habilidad."�\bEsto combina con su otra pasiva, que potencia sus siguientes ataques físicos y especiales cuando se aplica un nuevo clima, terreno o zona."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Psico-corte Neo, puede usarse siempre que haya un clima, terreno o zona activa. Siempre es crítico."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Acerola da +2 Defensa y +3 ratio de crítico a los Pokémon de su lado. Si hace sol (algo que su Tapu Bulu puede colocar), también da +2 Ataque."}\bAl entrar en combate, la primera pasiva de Bulu prolonga la duración del Campo de Hierba que coloca con su habilidad."�\bEsto combina con su otra pasiva, que potencia los siguientes ataques físicos de su lado cuando se aplica un nuevo clima, terreno o zona."{\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Danza Espada Inquebrantable, puede usarse siempre que haya un clima, terreno o zona activa."h\bDa +2 Ataque a Bulu y a sus aliados, y hace que sus siguientes ataques físicos hagan más daño."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Mina coloca Conjuro en su lado y da +4 At. Esp. (+6 si llueve) y Curación gradual a los Pokémon de su lado."�\bAl entrar en combate, la habilidad de Tapu Fini coloca una Zona Hada (porque Campo de Niebla es una basura) y prolonga su duración."�\bEsto combina con su otra pasiva, que da +1 Defensa y Defensa Especial a su lado cuando se aplica un nuevo clima, terreno o zona."�\bPor último, el Movimiento B de Fini, Protección de Deidad Marina, puede usarse siempre que haya un clima, terreno o zona activa."�\bAplica Protección a sí mismo y a sus aliados, luego restaura un 20% de PS (30% con Zona Hada) a sí mismo y a sus aliados, y devuelve las estadísticas bajadas a la normalidad si está lloviendo."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Gladion da +6 At. Esp., +3 ratio de crítico y potencia el siguiente movimiento especial de su Magearna."�\bMagearna tiene pasivas que bajan en -2 el At. Esp. del objetivo después de usar un movimiento y evitan que le bajen sus propias estadísticas."\bDespués, el Movimiento B de Magearna, Cañón Floral Perforante, solo puede usarse después de que haya usado un movimiento."{\bSu potencia y la del siguiente movimiento especial aumentan según cuánto se haya reducido el At. Esp. de los objetivos."?\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,Leon,Piers,Gloria (Dojo)]"�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Leon da +3 At. Esp. y +2 ratio de crítico a su Eternatus, pero le baja en -1 la Defensa Especial."�\bSu Eternatus también puede Eternamaxizarse y una de sus pasivas hace que Eternabeam no necesite un turno de recarga tras usarse."|\bSu otra pasiva también baja en -1 el Ataque, Defensa, At. Esp., Def. Esp., Velocidad, Precisión y Evasión del objetivo."b\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Piers da +2 At. Esp. y +2 ratio de crítico a su Toxtricity."�\bToxtricity tiene pasivas que colocan Campo Eléctrico y lo prolongan al entrar, además de ignorar los efectos de aguante del objetivo."{\bAdemás, tiene un Movimiento B, Sobremarcha de Ecos Dolientes. Solo puede usarse si hay un clima, terreno o zona activos."�\bTampoco puede bloquearse con Protección y hace más daño si el objetivo tiene un problema de estado, algo muy probable por Bomba Lodo."p\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Gloria da +3 Ataque a su Urshifu. Su Urshifu también puede Gigamaxizarse."s\bFuera de eso, simplemente tiene pasivas que bajan en -1 la Defensa y la Velocidad del objetivo al golpearlo."v\bCon Azote Torrencial, eso se aplica en cada golpe, ¡así que en realidad acabarás con -3 Defensa y Velocidad!"�\b¡Buena elección! Estos se hicieron para los aniversarios de PoMas y son mucho más sencillos comparados con los Neo Campeones."r\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,Lillie (2022),N (2022),Steven (2022), May (2023),Skyla (2023),Raihan (2023)]"x\bDato curioso: ¡esta es mi Entrenadora de aniversario favorita de todas! Su falda está taaaaan bien... ¡en fin!"�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Lillie da +6 At. Esp. y +3 ratio de crítico a su Lunala, siendo el primero de este tipo en PoMas."m\bSus pasivas colocan Viento Afín al entrar y potencian sus movimientos cuando tiene los PS al máximo."|\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de N da +3 At. Esp. y +1 Precisión a su Reshiram, además de colocar Viento Afín en su lado."�\bSus pasivas convierten sus movimientos de objetivo único en movimientos en área y bajan la Defensa Especial del objetivo después de golpearlo."_\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Steven da +2 Ataque y +3 ratio de crítico a su Rayquaza."{\bSus pasivas convierten las bajadas de estadísticas en subidas y le dan +1 Velocidad después de usar un movimiento."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de May da +2 Defensa, +2 Defensa Especial y +3 ratio de crítico a su Latias, además de colocar Viento Afín en su lado."�\bSus pasivas aumentan la probabilidad de efectos adicionales de sus movimientos y duplican las bajadas de estadísticas que provoca."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Skyla da +2 At. Esp. y +1 ratio de crítico a su Tornadus, además de dar +2 Velocidad a su lado."\bSus pasivas aumentan la probabilidad de efectos adicionales de sus movimientos y confunden al objetivo después de golpearlo."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Raihan da +4 At. Esp. y +2 ratio de crítico a su Flygon, y luego potencia los siguientes movimientos físicos y especiales de su equipo."�\bSus pasivas potencian los siguientes movimientos físicos y especiales de su equipo al usar un movimiento de estado, y cuando ataca a un objetivo que está retrocediendo, atrapado o confundido, le baja sus estadísticas ofensivas en -1."2\bPor último, su Flygon puede Dinamaxizarse."z\b¡Jo, jo! Todos estos tienen una Pasiva Máster (supongo que ya sabes lo que es a estas alturas) y un Movimiento B."~\bElige un Entrenador.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Calem,Marnie, Hop,Bede,Red,Leaf,Blue,Nate,Rosa,Silver,Cheren, Bianca,May,Brendan]"�\bSerena tiene bastantes cosas, así que vamos a dividir su kit en partes más pequeñas.\ch[2,-1,General, Agua,Siniestro,Movimiento B]"q\bSerena es bastante interesante. Cuando Greninja cambia de tipo por Mutatipo, también cambian sus pasivas."�\bLa parte más sencilla de su kit es sin duda su Movimiento de Entrenador. Da +2 Ataque, +4 At. Esp. y +3 ratio de crítico a su Greninja."?\bSu Greninja también tiene una Pasiva Máster Espíritu."�\bComo tipo Agua, Greninja tiene pasivas que maximizan el número de golpes de un movimiento múltiple y, por cada golpe, baja en -1 una estadística aleatoria del objetivo."b\b¡Eso significa que su Shuriken de Agua siempre acabará bajando tus estadísticas 5 veces!"�\bComo tipo Siniestro, Greninja tiene pasivas que bajan en -1 la Precisión del objetivo y tienen una probabilidad de hacerlo retroceder."p\bAtaque Rápido Sin Límites no activará Mutatipo, ¡así que Greninja no acabará siendo de tipo Normal!"�\bHace que el objetivo sea más débil al tipo actual de Greninja, además de bajar en -2 su Defensa y Defensa Especial y dar +3 Velocidad a su lado."�\bCalem tiene bastantes cosas, así que vamos a dividir su kit en partes más pequeñas.\ch[2,-1,General, Agua,Siniestro,Movimiento B]"g\bCalem está muy bien. Cuando Greninja cambia de tipo por Mutatipo, también cambian sus pasivas."�\bLa parte más sencilla de su kit es sin duda su Movimiento de Entrenador. Da +4 Ataque, +2 At. Esp. y ratio de crítico a su lado, y luego coloca Viento Afín."=\bSu Greninja también tiene una Pasiva Máster Orgullo."�\bComo tipo Agua, Greninja tiene pasivas que lo hacen inmune a los problemas de estado, además de restaurar PS al equipo cuando acierta un golpe bajo la lluvia."�\bComo tipo Siniestro, Greninja tiene pasivas que lo hacen inmune a las bajadas de estadísticas, además de restaurar PS al equipo cuando acierta un golpe en una Zona Oscura."r\bDoble Equipo Transformacional no activará Mutatipo, ¡así que Greninja no acabará siendo de tipo Normal!"t\bCuando Greninja es de tipo Agua, hará llover y potenciará los siguientes movimientos especiales de su lado."~\bSi es de tipo Siniestro, colocará una Zona Oscura y potenciará en su lugar los siguientes movimientos físicos de su lado."\\bY luego, sin importar el tipo, también dará +2 Evasión a Greninja y a sus aliados."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Marnie da +6 At. Esp., +4 Velocidad y +2 Evasión a su Moltres de Galar. Después, este recibe daño de retroceso equivalente al 10% de sus PS máximos."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Espíritu, sus otras pasivas le dan +3 ratio de crítico al entrar y potencian sus movimientos cuando no tiene los PS al máximo."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Ira Ígnea Feroz, solo puede usarse después de que se hayan usado otros 2 movimientos. No puede bloquearse con Protección y hace retroceder a su(s) objetivo(s)."}\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Hop da +3 Velocidad y -1 Defensa Especial a su Zapdos de Galar. Luego coloca una Zona Lucha."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Orgullo, sus otras pasivas le dan +2 Ataque al entrar y bajan la Defensa Especial del objetivo cuando le bajan la Defensa."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Patada Tronadora Rugiente, solo puede usarse después de que haya usado uno de sus otros movimientos. Baja en -3 la Defensa del objetivo."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Bede da +2 Ataque, At. Esp. y ratio de crítico a su lado, además de potenciar sus siguientes movimientos físicos y especiales."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Portaestandarte, sus otras pasivas dan +1 Velocidad a su lado al entrar y lo hacen inmune a los golpes críticos."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Mirada Glacial Intimidante, solo puede usarse después de que haya usado uno de sus otros movimientos. Da +1 Defensa y +1 Defensa Especial a su lado."|\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Red da +6 At. Esp. a su Articuno de Kanto y potencia su siguiente movimiento especial."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Espíritu, tiene unas cuantas pasivas más. Para empezar, sus movimientos siempre aciertan y siempre son críticos."�\bAdemás, reduce la resistencia del objetivo a los movimientos de hielo y potencia su siguiente ataque especial según a cuántos rivales haya golpeado su movimiento."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Rayo Hielo de Alas Heladas, solo puede usarse si un rival ha sido vuelto más débil a un tipo, y congela al objetivo."r\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Leaf da +6 Ataque, +6 At. Esp. y +3 ratio de crítico a su Moltres de Kanto."h\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Orgullo, sus pasivas potencian al máximo sus movimientos de estado."�\bAdemás de sus efectos originales, hacen que bajen en -1 el Ataque, At. Esp. y Defensa Especial del objetivo, y lo vuelven más débil a los movimientos de tipo Fuego."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Envite Ígneo de Alas Ardientes, solo puede usarse si un rival ha sido vuelto más débil a un tipo. Quema al objetivo y duplica sus bajadas de estadísticas."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Blue da +6 At. Esp. y +3 ratio de crítico a su lado, además de potenciar sus siguientes movimientos especiales."y\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Portaestandarte, sus pasivas hacen que sus movimientos sean extremadamente poderosos."�\bAdemás de sus efectos originales, vuelven al objetivo más débil a los movimientos de tipo Eléctrico y dan +1 Defensa y +1 Defensa Especial al lado de Zapdos."\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Respiro de Alas Tronadoras, solo puede usarse si un rival ha sido vuelto más débil a un tipo."�\bCura a Zapdos y a sus aliados un 60% y un 30% de sus PS máximos, respectivamente, da Curación gradual a su lado y elimina todos sus problemas de estado."~\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Nate devuelve a la normalidad las estadísticas reducidas de su Haxorus y le da +3 Velocidad."�\bCuando Nate usa su Movimiento de Entrenador, una de las pasivas de Haxorus también le da +6 Ataque y potencia su siguiente movimiento físico."l\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Orgullo, su otra pasiva hace que sus movimientos sean siempre críticos."u\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Enfado Negro Oscuro, solo puede usarse cuando el Ataque de Haxorus ha aumentado."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Rosa da una mejora a los movimientos especiales o físicos de su equipo cuando Meloetta está en Forma Lírica o Forma Danza, respectivamente."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Portaestandarte, sus otras pasivas giran en torno al hecho de que Meloetta tiene 2 formas distintas."r\bPara empezar, sus movimientos de tipo Normal pasan a ser del mismo tipo que el tipo secundario de Meloetta."�\bDespués de usar un movimiento, da +1 Defensa o +1 Defensa Especial a su lado (Danza y Lírica, respectivamente) y hace que el objetivo sea más débil al segundo tipo de Meloetta."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Canto Arcaico Maravilloso, solo puede usarse cuando Meloetta está a 1/3 o más de sus PS máximos."�\bCambia la forma de Meloetta, potencia los siguientes movimientos físicos y especiales de su lado y tiene una probabilidad de dormir al objetivo."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Silver da +6 Ataque y +3 ratio de crítico a su Tyranitar, además de +1 Precisión si se usa bajo tormenta de arena."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Orgullo, sus otras pasivas lo fortalecen bajo tormenta de arena. Para empezar, prolonga la duración de la tormenta."�\bSus movimientos también se potencian bajo tormenta de arena, y además recibe un aumento para su siguiente ataque físico después de atacar."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Avalancha Colosal, siempre hace retroceder a su(s) objetivo(s), pero no puede usarse de forma consecutiva ni en el primer turno de Ttar en combate."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Cheren da +4 Ataque y +4 At. Esp. a su Tornadus, además de potenciar sus siguientes movimientos físicos y especiales."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Espíritu, sus otras pasivas hacen que sus movimientos siempre acierten, sean críticos y luego potencien sus siguientes movimientos físicos y especiales."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Vendaval Negro Desolador, no puede usarse de forma consecutiva ni en el primer turno de Tornadus en combate."\bAumenta de potencia según cuánto se haya potenciado su siguiente movimiento físico y baja en -2 la Velocidad del objetivo."�\bAdemás, si se usa como el segundo movimiento de Tornadus tras entrar en combate, vuelve al o a los objetivos más débiles a los movimientos de tipo Volador."_\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Bianca da +4 Ataque y +3 ratio de crítico a su Virizion."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Portaestandarte, sus otras pasivas dan +1 Velocidad y Evasión a su lado después de usar un movimiento e ignoran los efectos de aguante."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Espada Santa de Luz Blanca, baja en -3 las estadísticas ofensivas del objetivo y lo vuelve más débil a los movimientos de tipo Lucha."I\bTambién ignora las subidas defensivas y de evasión del objetivo."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de May potencia el siguiente movimiento especial de un Pokémon de su lado y de su Kyogre, además de dar a este último +2 At. Esp."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Espíritu, sus otras pasivas le dan +2 At. Esp. al entrar y hacen que sus movimientos siempre acierten y sean críticos."�\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Pulso Primigenio Azul, solo puede usarse con Lluvia Intensa. Hace retroceder al o a los objetivos y baja en -3 su Defensa Especial."�\bEl Movimiento de Entrenador de Brendan potencia el siguiente movimiento físico de un Pokémon de su lado y de su Groudon, además de dar a este último +2 Ataque."�\bAdemás de su Pasiva Máster Orgullo, sus otras pasivas le dan +2 Ataque al entrar y hacen que sus movimientos siempre acierten y sean críticos."x\bPor último, su Movimiento B, Filo del Abismo Rojo, hace retroceder al o a los objetivos y baja en -2 su Defensa."�\bSin embargo, solo puede usarse bajo Sol Intenso y no puede usarse de forma consecutiva ni en el primer turno de Groudon en combate."w\bComo me di cuenta de que la dificultad del Desafío Sync fue un error, te he dado algunas mejoras para ayudarte."�\bBásicamente, dispones de mejoras por un valor de 7 puntos de energía. Hay 5 tipos de mejoras: Bendiciones, Inmunidades, Restauración, Potenciadores y Reductores."{\b¿Sobre qué tipo de mejora quieres saber más? \ch[1,-1,Bendiciones,Inmunidades,Restauración,Potenciadores, Reductores]"{\bLas Bendiciones dan aumentos de estadísticas a tus Pokémon al comienzo del combate y consumen energía según su nivel."�\bAdemás, puedes comprar una versión mejorada de la mejora (salvo la Bendición del Asesino) por solo unos pocos créditos más de los que tanto te ha costado ganar."�\bPor ejemplo, Bendición del Guerrero Nv. 1 dará +1 Ataque a tus Pokémon al entrar en combate, ¡como si tuvieran Espada Indómita!"�\bLas Inmunidades hacen que tus Pokémon sean inmunes a los problemas de estado, a las "interferencias" (es decir, retroceso, atrapamiento y confusión) o incluso a los golpes críticos durante un tiempo."k\bTodas consumen 2 puntos de energía y no pueden mejorarse más, como sí ocurre con las Bendiciones."�\bSin embargo, una vez que compres toda la tienda, podrás adquirir mejoras que te harán inmune a todos los problemas de estado y a todas las interferencias."F\bEso sí, consumirán 4 y 3 puntos de energía, respectivamente."�\bSi ahora hablas con la Enfermera Joy, ¡de verdad curará a tu equipo! Pero... solo un poco, si no le das nada de energía. Menos es nada, ¿no?"~\bDe base, curará a tu equipo un 10% de sus PS y restaurará 1/8 de sus PP (aunque al menos restaurará 1 PP por movimiento)."�\bSin embargo, las mejoras de Restauración aumentan esas cantidades. Por cada nivel de la mejora de Recuperación de PS, curará un 25%, 50% y 100% de los PS de tu equipo."�\bSin embargo, tus Pokémon debilitados solo recibirán un 10% de sus PS máximos, tengas o no una mejora de Restauración de PS. ¡Así que mantén con vida a tus Pokémon!"}\bPor cada nivel de la mejora de Recuperación de PP, restaurará 1/4, 1/2 y todos los PP de tu equipo, respectivamente."�\bAdemás, tampoco eliminará los problemas de estado de tu equipo; ¡primero tendrás que equipar la mejora Recuperación de Estado! Cuesta 3 de energía."�\bPor último, estas mejoras solo están activas en el Desafío Sync. Si diera curación en el Desafío Titán, ¡sería demasiado fácil!"�\bLos Potenciadores dan +1 a una estadística de tus Pokémon (excepto Precisión y Evasión) después de usar un movimiento, incluso aunque este falle."f\bTodos consumen 1 punto de energía y no pueden mejorarse más, como sí pueden las Bendiciones."|\bLos Reductores bajan en -1 una estadística del objetivo (excepto Precisión y Evasión) después de que sea atacado."~\bAdemás, no serán efectivos en el Desafío Titán; allí todos los rivales son inmunes a las bajadas de estadísticas."I\bOjalá pudiera participar en los eventos de Discord de Fire Ash..."g\bEn esos eventos podría conseguir mejoras de IV altos o quizá variocolor y legendarios raros..."\bVaya..."b\bPuede que haya perdido... ¡¡¡¡¡pero mi determinación sigue ardiendo con fuerza!!!!!!!"M\rEnfermera Joy: Parece que a tus Pokémon les vendría bien un arreglo."[\r¡Oh, bien! Tus Pokémon tienen un aspecto estupendo ahora. ¡Prepárate y cuídate!"_\r¡Oh, bien! Tus Pokémon tienen un aspecto estupendo ahora. Más suerte la próxima vez."'\b¡Fuera de los límites, chaval!")\rEstos desafíos te abren los ojos."`\rEse Inferno imponente, ese escalofriante Frío Polar. Y luego un aplastante Cometa Draco."_\r¿De dónde salen estos Entrenadores? Guau... Ojalá yo también pudiera ser como ellos.";\rConserje Joi: ¡Bienvenido al Club Grandeur Secreto!"o\r¡Numerosos Entrenadores de primer nivel, llegados de otras dimensiones, han venido a enfrentarse aquí!"3\rElige tu desafío: ¡te esperan recompensas!"W\rTambién puedes acudir a mí para recuperar tus Pokémon si pierdes tu desafío."\r¡Mucha suerte!"F\r¡Bienvenido de nuevo! Aquí tienes los Pokémon que te quedan."-\r¡No te rindas! ¡Vuelve a intentarlo!"4Presentador: ¿Vas a retirarte ahora? ¿Seguro?"$\bPresentador: Por favor, sube."\bEh, \PN."\\bAquí es donde te unirás con alguien de tu elección para enfrentaros a otros dúos."�\bLas combinaciones son infinitas y dependen de tu elección. Eso también significa que la victoria no depende por completo de ti."\bEmocionante, ¿verdad?"W\b¡Eh, compañero! ¿Te interesan algunos movimientos? Ya sabes, estos no los tienen en ningún otro sitio.\ch[98,-1,Celos,Instrucción,Gas Corrosivo,Ala Bis, Fuerza Expansiva,Ida y Vuelta,Fitoimpulso,Rencor Vivo,Rayo Meteórico,Bruma Explosiva,Poltergeist,Alto Voltaje,Escama Draco,Arenas Ardientes,Picadura,Allanador,Terrapulso,Triple Axel]"+\b¡Vuelve cuando quieras! O no. Jeje."\b¿Algún otro movimiento?\ch[98,-1,Celos,Instrucción,Gas Corrosivo, Ala Bis,Fuerza Expansiva,Ida y Vuelta,Fitoimpulso,Rencor Vivo,Rayo Meteórico, Bruma Explosiva,Poltergeist,Alto Voltaje,Escama Draco,Arenas Ardientes,Picadura,Allanador,Terrapulso,Triple Axel]"+\bOtro desafiante digno viene y se va."Z\bVeo tu entusiasmo y tu determinación inquebrantable. Deberías tener lo necesario."W\b¡No te rindas, muchacho! Igual que yo. Llevo aquí muchísimo tiempo. Jojojojo."JPOR FAVOR, INTRODUCE TU GC PAD PARA ACCEDER AL MENÚ DE LA GRAMOLA..."5¡BIENVENIDO [\PN]! POR FAVOR, ELIGE TU MÚSICA."&\ch[77,-1,Ritmos predeterminados]"{\ch[77,,Ritmos predeterminados,Violín primaveral,Flauta veraniega,Guitarra otoñal,Armónica invernal,Piano nocturno]"E\rEnfermera Joi: Esto es el Backstage, un lugar para prepararte."W\rTómate un descanso. Tómate un café. Pasa un momento por el baño. ¡Adelante!"D\rCuando estés listo, ¡sube arriba para tu próximo desafío!")\rQué fastidio. He vuelto a perder."=\rEs realmente difícil vencerlos con solo 3 Pokémon..."*\rENSÉÑAME. ¿CÓMO PUEDO GANARLES?"^\bEh, \PN, así que elegiste el Gauntlet, ¿eh? Entonces, ¿de qué quieres que te hable?"�\bEste desafío es sencillo. Básicamente, es un modo supervivencia. Sigue luchando contra tus rivales hasta que caigas. Así que no te desanimes ni te pongas triste por haber perdido. Lo diste todo."{\bPero hacerlo interminable parecía no tener salida, ¿eh? Así que dejé el límite en 100. Está bien saberlo, ¿verdad?"k\bUn último consejo: habla con la Enfermera Joy de vez en cuando, ¿vale? ¡Ahora en marcha! ¡Fuera!"I\bDéjame comprobarlo......\nTu racha actual de victorias es \v[81]."�\bUn. Combate. Más.\n¿Estás temblando de miedo? ¿Vibrando de emoción? ¿O vas a salir de aquí con la cabeza bien alta? En cualquier caso, lo has hecho genial. :) Haz una captura y búscame en Discord, ¡te has ganado el rol: [Gauntlet Maniac]!!!"�\bUrgh... Ya me estoy cansando de verte la cara. Es broma. Mira la hora. ¿Cuánto tiempo llevas ya? ¿Has comido? ¿Te has duchado? ¡Ya te queda muy poco!"�\bVaya, ¿sigues aquí? Debes de haber demostrado una determinación de verdad para llegar tan lejos. ¡Deberías hacer una captura de este momento y presumir de ello!"�\b¡Has superado la mitad del camino! ¡Felicidades! Entonces, ¿qué va a pasar ahora? ¿Es este tu final? ¿O vas a seguir avanzando por este ciclo aparentemente... interminable...?"�\bSinceramente, lo has hecho bien. Esta es una buena cifra para jugadores dedicados. Date una palmadita en la espalda. ¡Eso es!"s\bMuy bien, ¡has llegado bastante lejos! ¿Y qué haces aún aquí plantado? ¿Mmmm? ¿Echándote una siesta?"�\bVale, esto está bastante bien para jugadores casuales. Me gustaría darte las gracias por desafiar al Gauntlet y hacer que todo mi esfuerzo haya valido la pena. :)"�\bPuede que ahora mismo te estés encontrando con dificultades. ¿Quizá deberías farmear más en Practice y Club? ¡Canjea más recompensas para potenciar a tus Pokémon!"[\bDeja de mirar tu racha de victorias cuando puedes contarlas con una mano. En fin. :)"o\bDeja de mirar tu racha de victorias cuando ni siquiera necesitas una mano para contarlas. Madre mía. :)"e\bEh, \PN, veo que has decidido enfrentarte al Desafío Club. Déjame explicarte cómo funciona."|\bEl Desafío Club es en realidad solo un pequeño adelanto de lo que te espera en otras partes del Grandeur Club. Jejeje..."\bDependiendo de la dificultad que hayas elegido antes, te enfrentarás a cierta cantidad de Entrenadores. En Principiante serán 3 Líderes de Gimnasio; en Veterano, 4 Líderes y un miembro del Alto Mando; y en Experto, 5 Líderes, 2 miembros del Alto Mando y un "Campeón"."Q\b¡Al final, habla con Hitsu para recibir una recompensa por tus esfuerzos!"^\bEh, \PN, veo que has decidido enfrentarte al Desafío Club. ¿Quieres algunos consejos?"�\bPara empezar, quizá quieras plantearte usar movimientos con algo menos de potencia base, pero con más PP que los que usas ahora."}\bAsí no te quedarás sin PP en un movimiento y no perderás cobertura de tipos a mitad de combate, que es una faena enorme."*\b¿La fuente? Fíate de mí, colega."�\bDespués, deberías plantearte muy seriamente dar a tus Pokémon una buena distribución de EV. ¡Así no dejarás al rival con 1 solo PS!"|\bTambién podrías plantearte usar algunos movimientos de estado en lugar de abrirte paso a lo bruto por los combates."0\bEso es todo por mi parte, ¡buena suerte!"2\bBu. Bueno, da igual, suerte de todos modos."4Presentador: ¿Vas a retirarte ahora? ¿Seguro?"R\rDespués de pasarlo mal, por fin superé uno de los desafíos del Club. Uf."g\rNo me hagas caso. Solo estoy pensando qué Pokémon debería traer para mis próximos desafíos."P\bHola, esta es la entrada al DESAFÍO DE PRÁCTICA. ¿Te gustaría entrar?"z\b¿Y a qué región te gustaría desafiar? \ch[98,-1,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos, Alola,Galar,Hisui,Frente]"t\rEnfermera Joy: ¡Buenos días, \PN! ¡Espero que el Desafío Club no te lo esté poniendo demasiado difícil!"^\rLo siento si buscabas curación. Este servicio no está disponible en el Desafío Club."X\rEnfermera Joy: Buenos días, \PN. Tus Pokémon parecen estar bastante maltrechos."Z\rEnfermera Joy: Si quieres que te los arregle, voy a tener que cobrarte $1000000. :D"+\rJeje, ¿desesperado, eh? ¡Muy bien!"@\r¡Ahora todo está perfecto! ¡Cuídate! ¡Vuelve pronto!"V\r¡Eh! ¡No puedes permitirte mi servicio! ¡Cae debilitado y lárgate de aquí!".\rAwwww, ten cuidado ahí fuera. *guiño*"L\bJeje, ¡no paro de enfrentarme a Campeones! Menuda broma de desafío."�\b... eso diría, si no fuera porque solo fue un sueño que tuve anoche. En realidad, a mí solo me salen Líderes de Gimnasio. ¡AAAAAH!"[\b<i>Sollozos</i>. <i>Sollozos</i>... Mi equipo de Rattata... aniquilado. Waaaaaaaaaa~"�\bPues bien, este desafío diría que es EL MÁS COMPLICADO de todo el Grandeur Club. Así que escucha con atención. O también puedes ir y aprender a base de tropezar, caerte y darte de bruces."�\bEsto es básicamente un laberinto, un presidio, una ratonera. Eliges y entras por 1 de las 6 entradas, y tienes que escapar reuniendo 5 llaves. Las llaves las tendrán Entrenadores al azar, así que ya sabes, tendrás que derrotarlos para conseguirlas."�\bUna vez consigas las 5 llaves, todas las entradas pasarán a ser salidas, y solo tendrás que encontrar el camino para salir. ¿Lo has entendido todo ya? Te deseo mucha suerte. :)"�\bLuc-ker: ¡Ey, \PN! ¿Has venido a enfrentarte al Desafío Titán? Estoy deseando ver tu reacción ante los Entrenadores de aquí, jeje. ;)"�\bEn este desafío, además, tampoco podrás infligir a tus rivales problemas de estado, hacerlos retroceder, atraparlos o confundirlos."�\bPor último, movimientos cheese como Mismo Destino y Canto Mortal no funcionarán aquí; Desarme tampoco les quitará sus objetos. ¡No lo intentes!"y\bComo me di cuenta de que la dificultad del Desafío Titán fue un error, te he dado algunas mejoras para ayudarte."�\bSin embargo, tus Pokémon debilitados solo recibirán un 10% de sus PS máximos, tengas o no una mejora de Restauración de PS. ¡Así que mantén a tus Pokémon con vida!"~\bAdemás, aquí no serán efectivos en el Desafío Titán; todos los rivales son inmunes a las bajadas de estadísticas.""\bFoul: ¡Vaya, hola, colega!"\b¿Te has perdido?"�\b¿Te equivocaste de pasillo buscando el baño? Bueno, no te preocupes, sígueme y te llevaré de vuelta a donde se supone que debes estar."J\bAh, a quién voy a engañar. Los dos sabemos que no te has perdido."p\bEsta es una de las instalaciones más seguras de esta dimensión; la gente no se "pierde" aquí sin más."�\bParece que tu suerte se ha acabado, ya que te he encontrado yo antes que los otros dos. Verás, yo no soy tan amable como ellos...".\bAunque, por otra parte, estoy aburrido."\bEhhh, por qué no."�\bVerás, sería cruel si te derrotara ahora mismo, pero ¿no sería aún más cruel curarte solo para hacer que acabes cayendo más adelante?".\b¡Déjame enseñarte a qué me refiero!"E\bNada mal. Quizá sí tengas algo de talento, después de todo."N\bAhora lárgate y procura que no vuelva a pillarte merodeando por aquí."m\bPero quizá deja un currículum al salir. Puede que en el futuro necesitemos a alguien con tu talento."k\b¿Qué pasa, te sientes perdido? Es normal que un recién llegado se vea sobrepasado por este lugar."G\bBusca a Luc, él te dirá qué puedes esperar del Grandeur Club."p\b¿Cómo te va? Espero que el nivel de los Entrenadores del Grandeur Club no te haya pillado por sorpresa."\bBusca a Luc de vez en cuando para entender las reglas y normas de los distintos desafíos. Replantea tu equipo si hace falta."I\bSi te atascas, farmea y entrena. Lo conseguirás. ¡MUAHAHAHAHAHA!""\rEste desafío es rarísimo."F\rNo sé si estoy frenando a mi compañero o si pasa al revés..."F\r*suspira* Supongo que al final todo depende de la suerte, ¿eh?"#\b¿Completaste los desafíos?"A\bVeo salir de ahí a algunos Entrenadores de vez en cuando."/\bMe pregunto qué Pokémon habrán usado."\\rEnfermera Joy: ¡Buenos días, \PN! ¡Espero que lo pases bien en el Desafío Titán!"Y\rEnfermera Joy: Buenos días, \PN. Tus Pokémon parecen estar realmente maltrechos."~\rVermint: Hola, \PN. Espero que disfrutes tu estancia aquí. Intenta no pensar demasiado en nuestro primer encuentro, ¿vale?"P\rVermint: Hola, \PN. Había previsto que tendría que presentarme ante ti."t\rMi verdadero nombre es Vera. Creé tu vestuario y también estoy aquí para poner a prueba tu determinación."7\rEspero que esto no te resulte una sorpresa, \PN."gEl abismo es profundo y oscuro. Te estremeces al sentir las fuerzas abrumadoras que emanan de él."CCasi te desmayas. Sería buena idea mantenerse alejado de él."E\rEnfermera Joi: Esto es el Backstage, un lugar para prepararte."D\r¡Cuando estés listo, sube arriba para tu próximo desafío!"N\bNo me hagas caso, solo estoy preparándome mentalmente antes de entrar."=\b¡Ganarestavez,ganarestavez,ganarestavez,ganarestavez!"OUna Máquina Expendedora ominosa te observa fijamente. Mejor no acercarse."PPOR FAVOR, INTRODUCE TU GC PAD PARA ACCEDER A LAS MEJORAS SYGNA ENEMIGAS..."¡BIENVENIDO [\PN]!"pYa no parece que la Máquina Expendedora funcione. ¿Quizá solo puede usarse antes de empezar un desafío?"&La salida parece estar cerrada..."O\b¡Este es un lugar estupendo para subir a tus Pokémon hasta el Nv. 100!"I\b¡Hitsukid creó este desafío precisamente con esa idea en mente!"�\rHe oído el rumor de que hubo un tiempo en que este desafío no tenía dificultades y los Entrenadores se acumulaban encima de la Enfermera Joy."Y\rAterrador, ¿verdad? Me alegro de que eso ya no ocurra, si es que de verdad pasó."
\bAsh"\bLance"\bBrawly"l\bLuc-ker: Oh, ¿quieres combatir conmigo a plena potencia? Bien, pero no digas que no estabas avisado."R\bLuc: Demasiado fácil, ¿eh? Mentí: esa no era en realidad toda mi fuerza."�\bMi verdadero maestro, Yhwach, me concedió la letra V: The Visionary, ¡convirtiendo mi imaginación en realidad! Eso significa que puedo lanzarte cualquier cosa que sea capaz de concebir... y simplemente aún no he imaginado lo suficiente."\b¡Hasta la próxima!"r\bLuc: Jeje, eso ha sido solo una muestra de lo que está por venir. ¡Gracias por dejarme emplearme a fondo!"SEs una Máquina Expendedora. ¿Será como las demás del vestíbulo principal?"GPOR FAVOR, INTRODUCE TU GC PAD PARA ACCEDER A LAS MEJORAS SYGNA..."�TIENES \v[80] CRÉDITOS EN TU CUENTA. POR FAVOR, SELECCIONA UNA OPCIÓN. \ch[98,-1,Tienda de mejoras,Ver mejoras activas,Ver mejoras desbloqueadas,Añadir mejora, Quitar mejora activa,Borrar mejoras activas,Cerrar menú]"3YA HAS COMPRADO TODAS LAS MEJORAS DISPONIBLES."NO TIENES MEJORAS ACTIVAS."-NO TE QUEDAN MÁS MEJORAS DESBLOQUEADAS."(SE HAN BORRADO LAS MEJORAS ACTIVAS."wVaya, parece que no tienes suficientes Pokémon para combatir. Habla con la Enfermera Joy para que te los arregle."*\b¡Psst! ¿Quieres saber un secreto?"\bHe oído que Luc-ker estuvo a punto de volverse loco intentando traer aquí a Entrenadores de Passio para este desafío."`\bY vaya si le salió bien. Ahora tenemos estas monstruosidades disfrazadas de "desafíos"."4\b¡Ni siquiera son "desafíos", es puro abuso!"�\bSupongo que lo único que los salva es la existencia de las Bendiciones... una idea que le vino tras jugar demasiado a cierto modo roguelike de un juego en concreto."!\bJa, ja, tú te lo pierdes."F\r¿Sabías que hay una forma de llegar a las plantas superiores?"W\rHe oído que solo los Entrenadores fuertes o ciertos VIP podrán acceder a ello."�\r¿Cómo sabes si eres fuerte? Oí otro rumor: si llegas a destacar en Club, y me refiero a <i>destacar de verdad</i>, te reconocerán."A\rEspero que seas uno de los que lo consiga. ¡Mucha suerte!"t\rEnfermera Joy: ¡Buenos días, \PN! ¡Espero que el Desafío Dúo no te lo esté poniendo demasiado difícil!"^\rLo siento si buscabas curación. Este servicio no está disponible en el Desafío Dúo."V\r¡Eh! ¡No puedes permitirte mi servicio! ¡Cae debilitado y lárgate de aquí!"/\rHmm... ¿qué Bendiciones debería usar?"�\rPodría usar "Bendición del Asesino" para conseguir esa Velocidad extra y que mi Lucario pueda superar en Velocidad a casi todo..."�\bPero también necesito que pegue lo bastante fuerte, así que quiero la "Bendición del Guerrero"... ¿o debería pasarme a un set especial y usar la "Bendición del Brujo" para potenciar aún más a mi Regieleki...?"�\rAh, pero entonces no podría llevar Impasible para lidiar con lo que sea <i>eso<\i>... uf. ¿Quizá dejar una de mis Bendiciones en Nv. 2 entonces?"k\r¿Eh? ¿No sabes de qué estoy hablando? Ja, ja, ja. No has perdido contra ellos todavía, ¿verdad?"]\rO eres muy bueno, o aún no te han dado una buena paliza. Sea como sea, ¡diviértete!"0\bSolo el personal autorizado puede entrar."4\ch[98,-1,Mostrar tu Pase de Personal,Alejarse]"k\bOh, ¿eres parte del personal de aquí? Deberías haberme enseñado tu pase antes. Por favor, entra."%\bPor favor, márchate. Gracias."�\bFoul: ¡Hola! Me alegra ver que por fin has llegado. Por si no me reconoces, mi nombre es Foul Play at A Garbodor Price, pero mis amigos me llaman Foul."�\bSoy una de las pocas personas elegidas antes que tú para poner a prueba mi fuerza en este lugar. Y puedo decirte por experiencia que te lo vas a pasar muy bien... o no. Al final depende de ti."�\bSe ven toneladas de enormes recipientes experimentales que contienen especímenes flotando en líquidos coloridos y burbujeantes."D\bTío, me encanta este desafío a pesar de lo difícil que es."\bLos distintos Entrenadores a los que te enfrentas, sus mecánicas únicas, su estilo y hasta las Bendiciones que puedes usar."\bEs precioso. :')"H\bHola, esta es la entrada al DESAFÍO CLUB. ¿Te gustaría entrar?"J\bHola, esta es la entrada al DESAFÍO MAYHEM. ¿Te gustaría entrar?"�\bEn esta partida llevarás tu mochila, pero con una cantidad preestablecida de objetos. No te preocupes, recuperarás tu mochila original enseguida."9\bTienes un Pase Backstage. Déjame romperlo por ti."O\bQué raro. No parece que tengas un Pase Backstage. Intenta comprar otro."(\bPor favor, deja que te acompañe."�\bEn esta partida llevarás tu mochila, pero con una cantidad preestablecida de objetos. No te preocupes, recuperarás tu mochila enseguida."/\bSe ven curiosos especímenes de colores."F\bFuera de los lími...... ¿hmmmm? Déjame atender esta llamada."6\b¿Sí, señor? Sí. Sí. Está aquí. Recibido."K\bDisculpa. Ya puedes entrar y acceder a la planta superior. Adelante."G\b¡Espero que te lo estés pasando bien en el Grandeur Club, \PN!":\b¿Quieres refrescar lo que sabes sobre un desafío?"^\b¡Ey! Soy Luc-ker, ¡encantado de conocerte, \PN! (Por cierto, el guion es importante)."�\b¿Hmm? ¿Cómo sé tu nombre? Ajajá, no te preocupes por los detalles. Por cierto, puedes llamarme Luc si mi nombre completo te resulta demasiado complicado."o\bEn fin, estoy aquí para ayudarte dándote información sobre los desafíos, tal y como Hitsu me pidió."e\bMás te vale apuntarlo todo en un papel en vez de limitarte a machacar el botón de confirmar."^\bHay 6 desafíos principales en el Grandeur Club. ¿Sobre cuál te gustaría saber más?"{\ch[1,-1,Desafío Club,Desafío de Práctica,Desafío Gauntlet,Desafío Mayhem,Desafío Sync,Desafío Titán,Terminar]"[\bEl Desafío Club: aquí puedes combatir contra personajes de los juegos principales."�\bSi puedes combatir contra personajes del anime y de Pokémon Adventures, ¿por qué no hacerlo también con personajes de los juegos principales?"�\bTe enfrentarás a Pokémon de Nv. 90 en combates 3 contra 3. Si lo haces lo bastante bien, podrías conseguir algunos... *ejem* privilegios.".\b¿Hay algo más que te gustaría saber?"b\bEl Desafío de Práctica. Si el Desafío Club es demasiado difícil para ti, ¡prueba este!"�\bEs parecido al Desafío Club, pero los Pokémon están al Nv. 75 y no llevan objetos, así que es un buen sitio para entrenar a tus Pokémon."�\bEl Desafío Gauntlet, el desafío que te lanza Entrenadores encima hasta que tu equipo cae (o hasta que derrotes a 150 Entrenadores)."�\bTe enfrentarás a Pokémon de Nv. 100 en combates 3 contra 3, con beneficios a ciertos intervalos para ayudarte a construir tu racha de victorias."�\bTu mejor y más gloriosa racha quedará registrada para que puedas presumir de ella en Discord con otros jugadores, ¡así que saca la artillería pesada!"|\bEl Desafío Mayhem: aquí combatirás contra Entrenadores en combates completos, y todos sus Pokémon estarán al Nv. 100."�\bSi prestas atención, te darás cuenta de que, aunque te enfrentes al mismo Entrenador en otra partida, ¡su alineación de equipo casi nunca será la misma!"x\bEso es porque tienen una reserva de Pokémon esperando tu llegada. ¡Nunca sabrás qué se guardan bajo la manga!"j\bTambién tienen IV altos, así que más te vale traer a tus 6 mejores, ¡porque ESTO ES UNA LOCURA!"�\bEl Desafío Sync: combatirás contra Entrenadores con "Traje Sygna" (y otros atuendos) del popular juego para móviles "Pokémon Masters EX" en combates triples de 3 contra 3."�\bSus Pokémon también pueden tener mecánicas especiales, como no necesitar recargarse tras usar un movimiento de alta potencia base o no poder fallar ataques."P\bMás te vale traer tu amuleto de la suerte, ¡porque el desafío es real!"�\bEn el Desafío Titán combatirás contra Pokémon Sync, también conocidos como Titanes, en un combate triple de 6 contra 1. <s>Esto se hizo antes de Escarlata y Púrpura, mucho antes de que a alguien le pareciera genial.</s>"�\bMantendrán sus mecánicas del Desafío Sync, pero serán mucho más resistentes y no podrás depender de movimientos en área."�\bLa idea de Hitsu con esto es imitar el escenario de las incursiones de misión de ciertos RPG. Así que prepárate y ¡ve a por la cabeza!"2\b¡Uf! Gracias por eso. ¡Suerte ahí fuera!"\bPero qué demonios."w\bLlevé a mi Necrozma al Entrenador Extremo para maximizarle los IV. Tiene 252 EV en Ataque Especial. Es Modesto."�\b¡¡¡ENTONCES POR QUÉ DEMONIOS, DESPUÉS DE USAR ULTRAEXPLOSIÓN, SU MOVIMIENTO Z SOLO QUITA ENTRE UN 30 Y UN 35% A LOS POKÉMON DE MISTY???"\b¡¡¡ARGHHHHHH!!!"(\b¡Muéstrame lo mejor que tienes!"P\bBrock: El mundo es enorme. Aún hay muchos Entrenadores fuertes como tú."(\b¡Tengo fe en que los superarás!"S\rEnfermera Joy: Buenos días, \PN. Tu equipo parece estar bastante maltrecho."�\rLa unidad que tengo detrás se ha estropeado, así que no habrá más curación para ti durante el resto del desafío, para bien o para mal.")\r¡Vuelve otra vez la próxima vez!"V\rLa unidad está completamente cargada. Vamos a curar a tu equipo, ¿de acuerdo?"L\r¡Ya está todo perfecto! Sal ahí fuera y da lo mejor de ti, ¿vale?"n\rJeje, ¿desesperado, eh? Podría curarte con la unidad que tengo detrás, pero todavía no está lista."�TIENES \v[80] CRÉDITOS EN TU CUENTA. POR FAVOR, SELECCIONA UNA OPCIÓN.\ch[98,-1,Ver mejoras activas,¿Otras opciones?,Cerrar menú]"hLas otras opciones aparecen desactivadas. ¿Quizá solo puedan usarse antes de empezar un desafío?"\rUffffffffff."y\rO estos Titanes tienen una cantidad ridícula de PS y/o defensas, o nos están reduciendo el daño una barbaridad."Y\rEn fin. Sea como sea, de verdad parece que cada vez me enfrento a un jefe de JRPG."<\b¡Enhorabuena, has superado el DESAFÍO DE PRÁCTICA!"E\bAquí tienes tu recompensa, según la dificultad seleccionada."(\bSe te ha concedido 1 Crédito GC."=\b¡Vuelve a participar para conseguir más recompensas!"h\bPuedes salir siguiendo la señal con la flecha; es mejor no merodear por esta zona, ¿de acuerdo?"P\bNo, no, no. No más recompensas. Pero siempre puedes volver a intentarlo."4\b¡Enhorabuena, has superado el DESAFÍO CLUB!"*\bSe te han concedido 2 Créditos GC."*\bSe te han concedido 5 Créditos GC."*\bSe te han concedido 3 Créditos GC."+\bSe te han concedido 10 Créditos GC."+\bSe te han concedido 20 Créditos GC."8\b¡Enhorabuena, has superado el DESAFÍO GAUNTLET!"7\bAquí tienes tu recompensa, según tu recorrido."6\b¡Enhorabuena, has superado el DESAFÍO MAYHEM!"+\bSe te han concedido 25 Créditos GC."+\bSe te han concedido 50 Créditos GC."+\bSe te han concedido 75 Créditos GC."4\b¡Enhorabuena, has superado el DESAFÍO DÚO!"+\bSe te han concedido 15 Créditos GC."+\bSe te han concedido 40 Créditos GC."4\b¡Enhorabuena, has superado el DESAFÍO SYNC!"/\bSe te han concedido \v[61] Créditos GC."6\b¡Enhorabuena, has superado el DESAFÍO TITÁN!"^\rJe. No importa cuántas veces hagas este desafío, no habrá dos recorridos idénticos."u\rBueno, vale. Quizá sí la haya, pero es como una probabilidad del 0.000000000000000000000000000000000000001%."�\bEn serio. Hay tantísimos Entrenadores que sus equipos puede que ni siquiera sean los mismos cada vez, aunque te enfrentes al mismo Entrenador."�\rY ADEMÁS puede que ni siquiera aparezcan en el mismo orden ni en las mismas salas que en la partida anterior, aunque los Entrenadores sean los mismos."K\bAh, los desafíos de aquí son muchísimo más duros de lo esperado."5\bLa verdad es que me tiene bastante desanimado.""\b¿Y tú qué? ¿Te atreves?"B\b¿Qué tal va todo? ¡Seguro que lo estás haciendo genial!"H\bLo superarás y volverás a abrirte camino hasta aquí. ¿Verdad?"I\bHmm. Es muy difícil preparar una estrategia para cada Entrenador."�\bLa cuestión es que no existe un "lead perfecto". Podrías empezar con un Ferrothorn y te iría de maravilla contra Marlon, pero luego cualquiera de los Pokémon de Flint te lo tumbaría de un solo golpe."\bY entonces tendrías que malgastar objetos... o peor aún, quedarte con un Pokémon menos para el resto de los combates."L\r¡Guau, esto está delicioso! ¡Póngame otro para llevar, por favor!"�\rEnfermera Joy: ¡Buenos días, \PN! ¡Espero que estés aprovechando esta oportunidad para dejar a tus Pokémon en plena forma!"W\r..........espero que no hayas venido aquí buscando una curación rápida, ¿eh?"\\rVaya... Eh, este servicio no está disponible en el Desafío de Práctica. Lo siento."1\rHazlo lo mejor que puedas... ¿de acuerdo?"A\rEnfermera Joy: ¡Perfecto! ¡Ve a por esas victorias, \PN!"2\bEsto es inhumano. Creo que por hoy lo dejo."2\bMe despidieron de mi trabajo el mes pasado."�\bAhora no tengo nada mejor que hacer que farmear aquí. Mi mejor racha es de 70... la curación se vuelve mucho menos frecuente cuanto más avanzas."\\bHola, esta es la entrada al DESAFÍO GAUNTLET. Tu mayor racha de victorias es \v[93]."\b¿Te gustaría entrar?"A\bEste plato de curry es igual que mis desafíos en el Club."(\bME ESTÁ DESTROZANDO... *solloza*"9\bBwahahahaha. Yo... estoy temblando en esta planta."KPOR FAVOR, INTRODUCE TU GC PAD PARA ACCEDER AL MENÚ DE RECOMPENSAS..."k¡BIENVENIDO [\PN]! TIENES \v[80] CRÉDITOS EN TU CUENTA. POR FAVOR, ELIGE TU RECOMPENSA PARA CANJEAR."�\ch[98,-1,***OFERTA ESPECIAL***, Mejoras (1 Crédito),Alterificación (3 Créditos), Pack de BGM del Lounge (10 Créditos),Gemas (1 Crédito), Objetos equipables,Intercambio Crédito-Dinero]"\ch[75,-1, Código: Suerte (2 Créditos), Pase VIP Backstage (5 Créditos), Pase de Personal del Grandeur Club (500 Créditos)]"+¡POR FAVOR, RECOGE TU PAD! ¡GRACIAS!"GNO TIENES CRÉDITO SUFICIENTE. POR FAVOR, VUELVE EN OTRA OCASIÓN."-¡CANJE REALIZADO CON ÉXITO! ¡GRACIAS!"A¡EL PASE BACKSTAGE TODAVÍA NO ESTÁ A LA VENTA! ¡GRACIAS!"8¡EL PASE BACKSTAGE YA HA SIDO COMPRADO! ¡GRACIAS!"<YA TIENES UN PASE DE PERSONAL. VUELVE EN OTRA OCASIÓN."v\ch[75,-1,Tónico de Intensidad,Sérum de Vigor,Extracto Denso,Estimulante Oculto,Vacuna Apex,Pócima Relámpago]"o\ch[75,-1,Código: Aliento,Código: Grim,Código: Muro,Código: Tormenta,Código: Cúpula,Código: Brillo]"g¡EL PACK DE BGM DEL LOUNGE YA SE HA COMPRADO Y DESCARGADO! ¡POR FAVOR, RECOGE TU PAD! ¡GRACIAS!"P¡EL PACK DE BGM DEL LOUNGE SE HA DESCARGADO EN EL GRANDEUR PAD! ¡GRACIAS!"X\ch[98,-1,1 Crédito,2 Créditos,3 Créditos,5 Créditos,8 Créditos,10 Créditos ]"m\bEh, \PN, veo que has decidido enfrentarte al Desafío de Práctica. Déjame explicarte cómo funciona."�\bEl Desafío de Práctica es básicamente una versión más fácil del Desafío Club para que puedas subir de nivel a tus Pokémon y prepararte para él. En otras palabras, diseñamos este desafío para farmear."f\bEh, \PN, veo que has decidido enfrentarte al Desafío de Práctica. ¿Quieres algunos consejos?"Z\bLo siento, necesitas al menos 3 Pokémon capaces de combatir para el Desafío Sync."H\bHola, esta es la entrada al DESAFÍO SYNC. ¿Te gustaría entrar?"V\bPor favor, no me molestes. Necesito preparar una estrategia para los desafíos."OPOR FAVOR, INTRODUCE TU GC PAD PARA ACCEDER A TUS REGISTROS DE GRANDEUR..."B¿QUÉ REGISTROS QUIERES CONSULTAR? \ch[98,-1,Práctica,Club]"/Tus registros de Práctica están vacíos."*Tus registros de Club están vacíos."W¿QUÉ REGISTROS QUIERES CONSULTAR? \ch[98,-1,Práctica,Club,Gauntlet,Dúo,Mayhem]".Tus registros de Gauntlet están vacíos."*Tus registros de Dúo están vacíos.",Tus registros de Mayhem están vacíos."\\rEnfermera Joy: ¡Buenos días, \PN! ¡Espero que lo pases bien en el Desafío Mayhem!"Z\rEnfermera Joy: Si quieres que te los arregle, voy a tener que cobrarte $1000000. :D"T\rHe oído que aquí han llegado muchísimos más desafiantes de todo el mundo."P\r¡Eso me permitirá saber en qué punto estoy en mi camino hacia la cima!"Sí"No"Principiante"Veterano"Experto"Máster"Desafío"Recuento de victorias"Cancelar"Backstage"¿Sí?"
¡No!;[�"O\bMy head hurts trying to think about how to get through the challenges..."W\bDo I need high damaging moves? Or should I weaken them with tricks and statuses?"Y\bOr maybe I need to my Pokémons' EVs... or even worse, hunting high IV Pokémon..."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the DUET CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"8\bAnd what difficulty will you be participating in?"\bSure." \rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN!".\rWould you like to recieve some healing?"\r... and done! Ta-da!"o\rCan't believe you made me fully restore your team, you bastard. This wasn't supposed to even be a thing."`\rWhat, you expected a full heal? Haha, don't be ridiculous. This is already very generous."9\rYour team should already be at full health, right?"8\rHope you will have a good time in Sync Challenge!"1\bChoose your entrance. \ch[73,,A,B,C,D,E,F]")\bHmph, if this were a fist fight..."Q\bHi, this is the entrance for the TITAN CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"z\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Sync Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)")\bLuc-ker: You want some tips? Sure."�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto, Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary, Neo Champion,Sygna Buffs]"�\bThere's quite a few trainers here, so let's divide the trainers into their regions.\ch[98,-1,General Tips,Key Terms,Kanto,Johto, Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos,Alola,Galar,Anniversary,Neo Champion]"!\bGood luck, you'll need it."�\bAnd don't worry if you lose, you'll still get GC Credits for trying! That is, if you don't hit F12 because you're a sore loser or a tryhard."�\bYou want some general tips? Hmm. Best tip I can give here is to expect the unexpected. They don't play by the meta of the main series game, they play by PoMas's meta."�\bFor example, they'll buff their stats up by a lot more than they probably should, invent new mechanics, ignore Protect and heal more than they should, just to name a few things."�\bThey'll also have some interesting moves too, ranging from moves used by their trainers instead or powerful moves that can only be used under certain conditions."�\bFuthermore, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"�\bBut lastly, and you might find a silver lining in this - I've made it so that not only do you benefit from some damage reduction, the "harder" trainers have a lower chance to show up early."�\bSo if you want to familiarise yourself with the trainers here, it might be good to try this challenge with a lower difficulty first.".\bIn any case, good luck, you'll need it."�\bSure. Which one would you like me to explain? \ch[1,-1,Crit Rate,Trainer Move,B Move,Passive Skill, Master Passive,Zone,Gradual Healing]"R\bCrit Rate - how often a Pokémon lands a crit, up to a maximum of 3 stages."�\bTrainer Move - A move that the trainer uses (rather than their Pokémon). These moves tend to buff the user's Pokémon or their team's side."^\bThey can be used even when the trainer's Pokémon is afflicted with a status condition."}\bB Move - Stands for Buddy Move. You can identify them by the "descriptor" in the move's name, e.g. Origin Volt Tackle."~\bThey tend to do what the move they're based on does, but with increased power, added effects or the regular effect enhanced."\bThere's usually a condition that has to be met before each B Move can be used, so use that to your advantage to counter them!"�\bIf they don't, they will likely have very little PP instead. Lastly, all trainers only have 1 B Move at most, but there is 1 exception."mPassive Skill - Essentially an extra ability, but they can't be ignored by effects such as Mold Breaker."~\bHow many a Pokémon has is completely arbitrary, though I've tried to limit it to 3 at most, excluding Master Passives."l\bMaster Passive - A Passive Skill that increases the team's damage dealt and reduces the damage taken."k\bThere are 3 types: Flag Bearer is for all moves and is 10% damage increase and 20% damage reduction."W\bPride is for physical moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."_\bLastly, Spirit is for special moves and is 20% damage increase and 25% damage reduction."`\bZone - A field effect like a weather or terrain, boosting moves of a certain type by 50%."s\bGradual Healing - The Pokémon recovers 1/16th of their max HP every turn. Think of it kinda like Leftovers."T\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Brock,Misty,Erika, Red,Red (Thunderbolt),Blue,Leaf]"W\bBrock probably has the most basic kit here, since he's PoMas's first Sygna Suit."�\bAnyway, his Trainer Move give his Tyranitar's +1 Defense and makes its next attack guaranteed to land and crit, but there are ways to get around it, like Protect."�\bTtar has 2 passives. One gives its moves a higher chance to apply their additional effects and the other prevents its stats from dropping in a sandstorm."s\bMisty also has a very basic kit. Her Trainer Move gives her Vaporeon +2 Defense and her side +2 Sp. Defense."�\bLastly, her Vaporeon's passives give it gradual healing when switching in as well as a chance to raise its Evasion after it uses a move."}\bErika's Trainer Move gives her Leafeon's +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, but if the Sun's up, these stat increases are doubled."`\bLeafeon's ability is Chorophyll, so with the Sun up, her Leafeon's speed will be doubled."t\bThen, its passives don't allow status conditions to be inflicted on it as well as heal it after using a move."@\bIn other words, you really don't want Leafeon in the Sun!"�\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Charizard's +3 Attack, Sp. Attack and Speed and +2 Crit Rate, though its Defense and Sp. Defense are lowered by -1."{\bHis Charizard also has passives which allow its moves to never miss and not require a rechage turn after using them."X\bKnow what that means? It's able to use Blast Burn. Every. Single. Turn. Have fun!"s\bRed actually has a second Sygna Suit in PoMas. His Trainer Move gives Pikachu +6 Attack and Gradual Healing."�\bPikachu can also Gigantamax, though it maxes less use of it here compared to PoMas, since there you only use 1 Dynamax move for each sync pair per battle."h\bIt also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."{\bIts other passives make all its moves critical hits, as well as healing it after it uses a move in Electric Terrain."q\bLast, but certainly not least, Pikachu has a B Move which can only be used when Electric Terrain's active."X\bIf your Pokémon's paralyzed, its Defense and Sp. Defense are also lowered by -1."r\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Defense and +1 Crit Rate, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."~\bAnyway, his Blastoise is a tank of all time. When it's hit, one of its passive gives his side +1 Attack and Sp. Attack."�\bAnd then when it attacks, its other passive gives its side +1 Sp. Defense. Lastly, it also doesn't need to recharge after using Hydro Cannon."`\bWith Leaf's Trainer Move, I took a few creative liberties to make it live up to its name."q\bIt provides the Pokémon on her side Gradual Healing, as well as healing them all for 40% of their max HP!"�\bAs for Venusaur's passives, they badly poison your Pokémon and gives them -1 to their defensive stats after they're attacked by it."h\bWith Razor Leaf and a non-recharging Frenzy Plant, it's sure to deal out a ton poison and damage."Y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Morty,Ethan,Lyra,Kris, Silver,Giovanni,Giovanni (Ultra)]"q\bMorty's Trainer Move gives +1 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate to his side, as well as setting Tailwind."�\bOne of Ho-oh's passives gives additional stat boosts to its team if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."a\bIts other passive then heals the Pokémon on Ho- oh's side when it uses a move in the Sun."s\bEthan's Trainer Move powers up Lugia's next special move, gives it +1 Accuracy and makes its next move crit."{\bLugia has passives which makes its single target attacks hit all opponents as well as restore PP to Ethan's Trainer Move."k\bLastly, it also has a Spirit Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bLyra's Trainer Move gives +2 Attack and Sp. Attack to a Pokémon on her side and gives them Gradual Healing. But that's not the crazy thing about this sync pair."�\bCelebi has passives which leaves the opponent flinched, trapped and confused after using a move and lowers one of the target's stats by -2."v\bAnnnnd Celebi has Grassy Glide and can set up Grassy Terrain too to give it priority. Talk about a nasty combo!"j\bLastly, it also has a Pride Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."N\bIf you face her, pray that the other sync pairs are physical attackers."O\bAt base, her Trainer Move gives her side +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate."{\bBut if it's Raining, it also powers up the next special attack from her team, making them pack an even bigger punch."�\bOne of Suicune's passives gives its side +4 Sp. Defense if it successfully uses a status move the first time its used in battle."�\bIts other passive heals its team after a uses a move under the Rain. I think you get the idea - Rain is dangerous if you're facing Kris!"k\bLastly, it has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."k\bSilver's Trainer Move gives Sneasel +3 Attack and Speed, as well as setting up Tailwind on his side."�\bSneasel's B Move, Crushing Tripel Axel, can only be used when its HP is full. In theory, that doesn't sound too hard to counter, right?"\bWell, on every hit of a multi-hit move, its passives lower the opposing Pokémon's Speed by -1 while it gets +1 Evasion."~\bIt also gets +1 Crit Rate on each hit of its B Move too, but it doesn't have any other ways of increasing its damage itself."N\bSo at best, you get lucky and OHKO it, while at worst, it's a nuisance."<\bGiovanni's Trainer Move gives his Nidoking +6 Attack."a\bHis Nidoking has a passive to make all its attacks critical hits, including its Max Moves."�\bIts other passive turns Normal moves into Ground moves, allowing it to gain STAB from it. Its Mega Kick is going to hit pretty hard!"�\bThis version of Giovanni has a Trainer Move which gives his side +2 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as making Guzzlord the center of attention."{\bGuzzlord has passives which enable its Stockpile Defense and Sp. Defense boosts to be tripled and shared with its allies."O\bHowever, it can only Stockpile a maximum of 2 times as a result of this."�\bGuzzlord also doesn't have just 1 B Move, but 2! It's the one exception to the "rule" that says there can only be 1 B Move for each sync pair."i\bWhen used, they both remove Stockpiles's stat boosts and restores 1 PP to Giovanni's Trainer Move."�\bThe first one, Guzzling Swallow, can only be used after Stockpile has been used and restores Guzzlord's HP based on how many times it was used."=\bThen, it restores a fixed amount of HP for its allies."�\bThe second one is Gourging Crunch. It can only be used when the Guzzlord's stat boosts for Defense and Sp. Defense are 6 or greater."9\bIt then lowers the target's defensive stats by -1.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,May,Brendan,Steven,Wally]"�\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Blaziken +4 Attack and +1 Accuracy, sets up Tailwind and protects it from damage for the rest of the turn."�\bBlaziken's first passive gives +1 Speed to its side when entering battle, including Mega Evolution, effectively translating to a +2 increase."�\bIts other passive lowers the target's Defense by -2. All in all, very speedy and it can easily snowball if you're not careful."c\bBrendan's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense as well as +1 Crit Rate."u\bHis Latios's first passive powers up its sides' next special moves when entering the battle and Mega Evolving."x\bIts other passive then increases the likelihood of additional effects; if it's a stat drop, it'll be doubled too."p\bIt has Luster Purge, so that'll mean that you'll be taking a lot of special damage if you're not careful!"�\bSteven... is a lot. Because he has a Deoxys, PoMas decided to give him not just 1 form of Deoxys, but all 4! So let's break him down a bit.\ch[2,-1,Initial State,Shared Traits, Normal Forme,Attack Forme,Defense Forme,Speed Forme]"\bInitially, Deoxys starts in its Normal Forme with 4 Trainer Moves and a passive which gives it +1 Accuracy when switching in."�\bThe first one, "Try This!", sets Psychic Terrain and gives Deoxys +2 Defense, Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Speed and keep Deoxys in its Normal Forme."u\bHis second one, "Attack!", gives Deoxys +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, then changes Deoxys into Attack Forme."�\bThe third one, "Defend!" gives its +4 side Attack and Sp. Attack. Deoxys then changes into its Defense Form and protects itself from damage for the rest of the turn."r\bLast but not least,"Faster!", gives Deoxys +6 Speed and +3 Evasion and changes Deoxys into its Speed Forme."�\bOutside of its inital state, all forms of Deoxys that Steven has have a passive with converts stat drops into stat increases, but not vice versa like Contrary does!"a\bThey all also have Psycho Boost and Zen Headbutt, so I won't be mentioning them elsewhere."`\bIn its Normal Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."{\bIt also has a passive which increase the chance of additional effects, so if it uses Zen Headbutt, be prepared to flinch!"`\bIn its Attack Forme, Deoxys has Protect and Cosmic Power in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which increases the power of its next physical and special moves, so it might quickly snowball out of control!"a\bIn its Defense Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Iron Defense in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which gives its side +2 Sp. Defense each time a status move is used, so with Iron Defense it'll become very bulky very quickly."^\bIn its Speed Forme, Deoxys has Recover and Double Team in addition to the common moves."�\bIt also has a passive which sets up Tailwind for its side when a status move is successful the first time it's used in battle."_\bWally's Trainer Move gives his Gardevoir +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Sp. Defense and Crit Rate."�\bGardevoir has 2 passives - the first gives its side +1 Speed when entering battle and Mega Evolving; the other leaves the target confused after a move."�\bGardevoir also has a B Move, Ultimate Dazzling Gleam. It lowers the targets' Attack and Sp. Attack by -4, then makes them weaker to Fairy type attacks."�\bIt can only be used once, but you can't Protect against it and -4 on your attacking stats will likely force you to switch out your Pokémon."V\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Cynthia,Cynthia (Renegade),Cynthia (Aura),Cyrus,Dawn]"�\bCynthia's Trainer Move, which I took some creative liberties with, raises her Kommo-o's Crit Rate and boosts its next special attack depending on how low its HP is."�\bApart from that, Kommo-o has passives which allow it to ignore damage reduction from Reflect, Light Screen and Aurora Veil as well as increase the chance for additional effects."�\bThis version of Cynthia's Trainer Move gives Giratina +4 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate. She can also set a Ghost Zone."T\bHer Giratina's attacks lower the Defense and Sp. Defense of the target by -1."�\bThis Cynthia's Trainer Move gives her side +4 Defense and Sp. Defense, but if a Fighting Zone is active, she'll give +6 instead."r\bAs for that, her Lucario has a passive which sets Fighting Zone on entry, so most of the time, it'll be +6."s\bLucario's other passive also depends on Fighting Zone - it heals its side after using a move if it's active."y\bIt also has Superior Aura Sphere, a B Move that never misses and can only be used after Lucario is attacked twice."]\bAfter it deals damage, it powers up the next physical and special attacks of its side."p\bLastly, Lucario has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."\bCyrus's Trainer Move gives his Darkrai +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy and Crit Rate. In addition, he can set a Dark Zone."�\bDarkrai has passives which power up its moves if the target is asleep, or if it's using a status move, it'll lower a random stat of all opponents by -1."[\bIt does have Dark Void, but even if it misses, its 2nd passive will activate anyway."�\bDawn's Trainer Move gives her side +2 Defense, Sp. Defense and Crit Rate, but her Cresslia takes recoil damage equal to 30% of its remaining HP."^\bYou might be thinking, why do that, when most other trainer moves don't have downsides?"i\bCresselia's very tanky, but one of its passives makes it even more so when it has 50% HP or lower."�\bIts other passive also increases the power of its side's special moves if Cresselia uses a status move when it's HP is 50% or lower."P\bIt also has Moonlight for healing, so don't count your chickens too soon!"R\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Elesa,Grimsley,Hilbert,Hilda,N, Roxie,Ingo,Emmet]"�\bElesa's Trainer Move gives +2 Accuracy and Crit Rate to a Pokémon on her side, as well as giving +2 Sp. Attack to all Pokémon on her side."�\bRotom has a passive which gives it +1 Evasion when it's hit, as well as another which prevents its Evasion from being lowered."�\bGrimsley's Trainer Move makes his Sharpedo take recoil damage equal to 90% of its remaining HP, but in return it gives +6 Attack and Evasion and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition, it has passives which increase the chance of the additional effects its moves and increase their power when Sharpedo is in a pinch."s\bHilbert's Trainer Move gives his Genesect +3 Sp. Attack, +2 Crit Rate and powers up its next special attack."�\bWhen using Techno Blast, Genesect changes form depending on the type the target is weakest to. Its default is also Bug instead of Normal."]\bThen, it makes them weaker to that type and applies an effect corresponding that type."m\bElectric - Paralyze target.\n Fire - Lower target's Attack by -1.\n Ice - 50% chance to freeze target."H\bWater - Lower target's Defense by -1. Bug - No additional effect."d\bLastly, if Genesect lands a super effective hit, its passive lowers the target's Speed by -2."�\bHilda's Trainer Move raises her Victini's Sp. Attack by how much its Attack has been raised, then gives it +3 Crit Rate and gives its team +1 Accuracy."�\bThis is complemented by Victini's passives, which gives it +2 Attack on switching in and turns stat drops into stat increases."y\bThere's even more synergy - Victini has V-Create, so it just keeps getting bulkier and faster each time it's used!"D\bN's Trainer Move gives his Kyurem +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bWhen Kyurem uses charges up to use Freeze Shock, it has a passive which halves the damage it takes while charging and unlocks its B Move, Resonating Noble Roar."|\bIt lowers the Attack, Sp. Attack, and Speed of all opposing Pokémon by -2, while it powering up its next physical attack."�\bFreeze Shock then needs to be used again before it can be used again, preventing it from being spammed endlessly (it also has 3 PP)."�\bKyurem also has a passive which allows it to ignore the opponent's enduring effects, but I imagine that won't come up too often."q\bRoxie's Trainer Move gives her Toxtricity +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate and applies Tailwind to her side."W\bToxtricity has has 2 passives. One sets Poison Zone on switch in and extends it."e\bThe other lowers the target's Attack or Sp. Attack if it's poisoned or paralyzed respectively."~\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Frenzied Sludge Wave. It can only be used if there's an opponent with a status condition."�\bIt can't be protected against, lowers the target's Sp. Defense by -2 and poisons it if it doesn't already have a status condition."^\bIngo's Trainer Move gives his side +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. His Chandelure can Dynamax."�\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as increasing the power of its team's next special moves."�\bIt also has a B Move, Rising Flames Hex. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."�\bIt applies effects based on what the target's inflicted with:\nParalysis - Lower target's Defense by -2.\n Burn - Lower target's Sp. Defense by -2."^\bPoison - Heal itself and allies for a little HP.\n Flinch - Lower target's Speed by -2."b\bTrap - Power up user's next physical move.\n Confusion - Power up user's next special move."�\bEmmet's Trainer Move gives a Pokémon on his side Ground immunity for 5 turns and makes its next moves critical hits. His Eelektross can Dynamax."m\bAfter it uses a move, its passives give it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as trapping the target."�\bIt also has a B Move, Descending Lightning Wild Charge. It can only be used if there is an opponent with a status condition, or is flinching, trapped or confused."A\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Korrina,Diantha,Lysandre]"g\bSerena's Trainer Move gives her +6 Zygarde's Attack and Sp. Attack and gives it Gradual Healing."\\bZygarde's passives prevent its stats from being lowered and its attacks from missing."p\bLastly, it also has a Flag Bearer Master Passive. Refer to the Key Terms section to know what that means."�\bKorrina's Trainer Move gives her Marshadow +4 Attack and +3 Speed and Evasion. After attacking, Marshadow's passive raises one of its stats by +1 3 times."|\bIf her Diancie's Defense has been raised, Diantha's Trainer Move raises its Sp. Defense by the same amount of stages."`\bThen, it gives Diancie Gradual Healing and makes its next physical attack do more damage."x\bDiancie's B Move, Pink Diamond Storm, can only be used when there's a Rock Zone active, which Diantha can set up."M\bIt lowers the target's Defense by -2 while giving its side +2 Defense."�\bDiancie's passives lower all opponents' Speed by -1 when entering battle and Mega Evolving, as well as giving it +2 Attack and +1 Crit Rate after using a move."_\bLysandre's Trainer Move gives his +4 Volcanion Sp. Attack, +1 Accuracy and +3 Crit Rate."�\bVolcanion itself has one passive which burns the targets that it hits. This is then complimented with its B Move, Heat Hydro Pump."�\bIt can only be used when at least one opposing Pokémon is burned and is an AoE move which deals more damage to burned targets."o\bThen, based on how many burned targets it hits, it makes Volcanion's next special attack do more damage."I\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lusamine,Hau,Lana, Acerola,Mina,Gladion]"v\bLusamine's Trainer Move gives Necrozma +6 Sp. Attack and -1 Speed. Her Dusk-Mane Necrozma can also Ultra Burst."�\bIt also has passives which turns its single target moves into AoE moves and allows Prismatic Laser to be used without the user recharging."M\bHau's Trainer Move gives his Tapu Koko +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."z\bWhen entering battle, one of Koko's passives extends the duration of the Electric Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next special attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."l\bThen, Koko's B Move, Wild Electroweb, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt doubles in power when a Fairy Zone is active (which Hau can set up) and lowers the Speed of all targets by -2 while +2 Speed to Koko and its allies."H\bLana's Trainer Move gives her Tapu Lele +6 Attack and Sp. Attack."y\bWhen entering battle, one of Lele's passives extends the duration of the Psychic Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up its next physical and special attacks when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."{\bLastly, its B Move, Neo Psycho Cut, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active. It always crits."�\bAcerola's Trainer Move gives +2 Defense and +3 Crit Rate to her side's Pokémon. If it's Sunny (which her Tapu Bulu can set up), it gives +2 Attack too."v\bWhen entering battle, Bulu's first passive extends the duration of the Grassy Terrain it sets with its ability."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which powers up the next physical attacks from its side when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."t\bLastly, its B Move, Unbreakable Swords Dance, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."b\bIt gives +2 Attack to Bulu and its allies makes their next physical attacks do more damage."�\bMina's Trainer Move sets up Lucky Chant on her side and gives +4 Sp. Attack (+6 if Raining) and Gradual Healing to the Pokémon on her side."x\bWhen entering battle, Tapu Fini's ability sets Fairy Zone (because Misty Terrain sucks) and extends its duration."�\bThis then combos with its other passive, which gives its side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense when a new weather, terrain or zone is applied."p\bLastly, Fini's B Move, Sea Deity Protect, can be used whenever there's a weather, terrain or zone active."�\bIt applies Protect to itself and its allies, then it restores 20% HP (30% with Fairy Zone) for itself and its allies and returns lowered stats back to normal if it's Raining."q\bGladion's Trainer Move gives his Magearna +6 Sp. Attack, +3 Crit Rate and powers up its next special move."�\bMagearna has passives which lower the target's Sp. Attack by -2 after using a move and prevent its own stats from being lowered."]\bThen, Magearna's B Move, Piercing Fleur Cannon, can only be used after it uses a move."}\bIts power and the power of its next special move increases based on how much the targets' Sp. Attack has been lowered.":\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Leon,Piers,Gloria (Dojo)]"o\bLeon's Trainer Move gives his Eternatus +3 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate but lowers its Sp. Defense by -1."�\bHis Eternatus is also able to Eternamax and one of its passives enables its Eternabeam to not require a recharge turn after it's used."~\bIts other passive also lowers the target's Attack, Defense, Sp. Attack, Sp. Defense, Speed, Accuracy and Evasion by -1."O\bPier's Trainer Move gives his Toxtricity +2 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate."�\bToxtricity has passives which set Electric Terrain and extend it on switch in, as well as ignore the target's enduring effects."}\bIn addition, it has a B Move, Sorrowful Echos Overdrive. It can only be used if there's an active weather, terrain or zone."�\bIt also can't be protected against and does more damage if the target has a status condition, which would most likely happen from its Sludge Bomb."Z\bGloria's Trainer Move gives her Urshifu +3 Attack. Her Urshifu can also Gigantamax."p\bOther than that, it just has passives which lower the target's Defense and Speed by -1 when hitting them."j\bWith Surging Strikes, it'll apply to each hit, so you'll actually end up with -3 Defense and Speed!"v\bNice choice! These guys were made for PoMas's anniversaries and are much simpler compared to the Neo Champions."m\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Lillie (2022),N (2022),Steven (2022), May (2023),Skyla (2023),Raihan (2023)]"l\bFun fact: This is my favourite anniversary trainer out of them all! Her skirt is sooo good... anyway!"m\bLillie's Trainer Move gives her Lunala +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, the first of its kind in PoMas."b\bIts passives set Tailwind when its switched in and powers up its moves when its HP is full."r\bN's Trainer Move gives his Reshiram +3 Sp. Attack and +1 Accuracy, as well as setting Tailwind on his side."v\bIts passives turn its single target moves into AoE moves and lower the target's Sp. Defense after attacking it."K\bSteven's Trainer Move gives his Rayquaza +2 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."a\bIts passives turn stat drops into stat increases and gives it +1 Speed after using a move."{\bMay's Trainer Move gives her Latias +2 Defense and Sp. Defense and +3 Crit Rate, as well as setting Tailwind on her side."s\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and doubles stat drops that it inflicts."s\bSkyla's Trainer Move gives her Tornadus +2 Sp. Attack and +1 Crit Rate, as well as giving her side +2 Speed."v\bIts passives increase the likelihood of additional effects of moves and confuses the target after attacking it."�\bRaihan's Trainer Move gives his Flygon +4 Sp. Attack and +2 Crit Rate, then powers up his team's next physical and special moves."�\bIts passives power up its team's next physical and special moves when using a status move and when attacking a target that's flinching, trapped or confused, it lowers its attacking stats by -1."&\bLastly, his Flygon can Dynamax."n\bHoho! All of these guys have a Master Passive (I'm assuming you know what that is by now) and a B Move."y\bPick a trainer.\n\ch[1,-1,Serena,Calem,Marnie, Hop,Bede,Red,Leaf,Blue,Nate,Rosa,Silver,Cheren, Bianca,May,Brendan]"w\bSerena has quite a lot going on, so let's split her kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"n\bSerena is quite interesting. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."\bThe simplest part of her kit is definitely her Trainer Move. It gives her Greninja +2 Attack, +4 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."5\bHer Greninja also has a Spirit Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which max out the number of hits of a multi-strike move and for each hit, it lowers a random stat of the target by -1."T\bThat means its Water Shuriken will always end up lowering your stats 5 times!"z\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which lower the target's Accuracy by -1 and has a chance of making it flinch."b\bBoundless Quick Attack won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"�\bIt makes the target weaker to Greninja's current type, as well as lower its Defense and Sp. Defense by -2 and give its side +3 Speed."v\bCalem has quite a lot going on, so let's split his kit into smaller chunks.\ch[2,-1,General, Water,Dark,B Move]"g\bCalem is pretty cool. When Greninja changes type due to Protean, it'll also change its passives."�\bThe simplest part of his kit is definitely his Trainer Move. It gives his side +4 Attack, +2 Sp. Attack and Crit Rate, then sets up Tailwind."4\bHis Greninja also has a Pride Master Passive."�\bAs a Water type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to status conditions, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in the rain."�\bAs a Dark type, Greninja has passives which make it immune to stat drops, as well as restoring HP for the team when it lands a hit in a Dark Zone."h\bTransformational Double Team won't trigger Protean, so Greninja won't end up being a Normal type!"c\bWhen Greninja's a Water type, it'll make it rain and power up its side's next special moves."i\bIf it's a Dark type, it'll set up a Dark Zone and power up its side's next physical moves instead."S\bThen regardless of type, it'll also give Greninja and its allies +2 Evasion."�\bMarnie's Trainer Move gives her Galarian Moltres +6 Sp. Attack, +4 Speed and +2 Evasion. It then takes 10% of its max HP as recoil damage."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives give it +3 Crit Rate when switching in and powers up its moves when it's not at max HP."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fierce Fiery Wrath, can only be used after 2 other moves have been used. It can't be protected against and flinchest its target(s)."q\bHop's Trainer Move gives his Galarian Zapdos +3 Speed and -1 Sp. Defense. It then sets up a Fighting Zone."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives give it +2 Attack on entry and lower the target's Sp. Defense when lowering its Defense."�\bLastly, its B Move, Roaring Thunderous Kick, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It lowers the target's Defense by -3."�\bBede's Trainer Move gives his side +2 Attack, Sp. Attack and Crit Rate, as well as powering up his side's next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives give its side +1 Speed on entry and makes it immune to critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Intimidating Freezing Glare, can only be used after one of its other moves has been used. It gives his side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."i\bRed's Trainer Move gives his Kantonian Articuno +6 Sp. Attack and powers up its next special move."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, it has quite a few other passives. First off, its moves will always land and be critical hits."�\bThen, it lowers its target's resistance to ice moves and powers up its next special attack based on how many opponents its move hit."�\bLastly, its B Move, Frozen Wings Ice Beam, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type and freezes the target."a\bLeaf's Trainer Move gives her Kantonian Moltres +6 Attack and Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate."Z\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its passives supercharge its status moves."�\bIn addition to their original effects, it makes them lower the target's Attack, Sp. Attack and Sp. Defense by -1 and makes it weaker to Fire moves."�\bLastly, its B Move, Fiery Wings Flare Blitz, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type. It burns the target and double its stat drops."z\bBlue's Trainer Move gives his side +6 Sp. Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as powering up their next special moves."^\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its passives make its moves very potent."�\bIn addition to their original effects, they make the target weaker to Electric moves and give Zapdos's side +1 Defense and Sp. Defense."r\bLastly, its B Move, Thundering Wings Roost, can only be used if an opponent has been made weaker to a type."�\bIt heals Zapdos and its allies for 60% and 30% of their respective max HPs, gives its side Gradual Healing and removes all their status conditions."d\bNate's Trainer Move returns his Haxorus's lowered stats back to normal and gives it +3 Speed."~\bWith Nate using his Trainer Move, one of Haxorus's passives will also give it +6 Attack and power up its next physical move."`\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passive makes its moves critical hits."f\bLastly, its B Move, Dark Black Outrage, can only be used when Haxorus's Attack has been raised."�\bRosa's Trainer Move gives her side a boost to her team's special or physical moves when Meloetta is in its Aria or Pirouette forms respectively."}\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives play around the fact that Meloetta has 2 different forms."U\bFirst off, its Normal moves become the same type as Meloetta's secondary type."�\bAfter using a move, it then give its side +1 Defense or Sp. Defense (Pirouette and Aria respectively) and makes its target weaker to Meloetta's second type."p\bLastly, its B Move, Relic Song of Wonder, can only be used when Meloetta is at 1/3 or more of its max HP."�\bIt changes Meloetta's form and powers up its side's next physical and special moves and has a chance to make the target fall asleep."{\bSilver's Trainer Move gives his Tyranitar +6 Attack and +3 Crit Rate, as well as +1 Accuracy if used in a Sandstorm."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives strengthen it in a Sandstorm. First, it extends the duration of Sandstorms."\bIts moves also get powered up in a Sandstorm and it also gets a boost to its next physical attack after using an attack."�\bLastly, its B Move, Massive Rock Slide, always flinches its target(s) but can't be used consecutively or on Ttar's first turn in battle."�\bCheren's Trainer Move gives his Tornadus +4 Attack and Sp. Attack, as well as powering it its next physical and special moves."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives make its moves always land, be critical hits, then strengthen its next physical and special moves."y\bLastly, its B Move, Black Gale Bleakwind Storm, can't be used consecutively or on Tornadus's first turn in battle."}\bIt increases in power based on how much its next physical move would be powered up and lower the target's Speed by -2."}\bIn addition, if it's used as Tornadus's 2nd move after entering battle, it makes the target(s) weaker to Flying moves."K\bBianca's Trainer Move gives her Virizion +4 Attack and +3 Crit Rate."�\bIn addition to its Flag Bearer Master Passive, its other passives allow gives its side +1 Speed and Evasion after using a move and ignore enduring."�\bLastly, its B Move, White Light Sacred Sword, lowers the target's attacking stats by -3 and makes its weaker to Fighting moves."A\bIt also ignores the target's defensive and evasive boosts."�\bMay's Trainer Move powers up the next special move of a Pokémon on her side and her Kyogre, as well as giving the latter +2 Sp. Attack."�\bIn addition to its Spirit Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Sp. Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."�\bLastly, its B Move, Blue Origin Pulse, can only be used in Heavy Rain. It lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Sp. Defense by -3."�\bBrendan's Trainer Move powers up the next physical move of a Pokémon on his side and his Groudon, as well as giving the latter +2 Attack."�\bIn addition to its Pride Master Passive, its other passives allow gives it +2 Attack on entry and make its moves always land and be critical hits."v\bLastly, its B Move, Red Precipice Blades, lowers the makes the target(s) flinch and lowers their Defense by -2."v\bHowever, it can only be used in Harsh Sun and can't be used consecutively or on Groudon's first turn in battle."z\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Sync Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bEssentially, you have 7 energy worth of buffs. There are 5 types of buffs: Blessings, Immunities, Restoration, Boosters and Crushers."q\bWhat buff type would you like to know about? \ch[1,-1,Blessings,Immunities,Restoration,Boosters, Crushers]"\bBlessings give your Pokémon stat increases at the start of a battle and they use energy corresponding with their level."�\bIn addition, you can buy an enhanced version of the buff (apart from the Assasin's Blessing) for just a few more of your hard-earned credits."�\bAs an example, Warrior's Blessing Lv. 1 will give your Pokémon +1 Attack when they enter battle, essentially giving them Intrepid Sword!"�\bImmunites make your Pokémon immune to status conditions, "interferences" (i.e. flinching, trapping and confusion) or even critical hits for some time."Q\bAll of them use 2 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."�\bHowever, once you buy out the whole store, you can then buy buffs that make you immune to all status conditions and interferences."<\bThey will use up 4 and 3 energy respectively, though."�\bIf you talk to Nurse Joy now, she'll actually heal your team now! But... just a little bit, if you don't give her any energy. Better than nothing though, amirite?"�\bAt base, she'll heal your team for 10% of its HP, as well as restore 1/8 of its PP (restoring at least 1 PP per move, though)."�\bThe restoration buffs increase those amounts though. For each level of the HP Recovery buff, she'll heal 25%, 50% and 100% of your team's HP."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your 'mons alive!"m\bFor each level of the PP Recovery buff, it'll restore 1/4, 1/2 and all of your team's PP respectively."�\bFurthermore, she also won't remove status conditions from your team; you'll have to equip the Status Recovery buff first! It costs 3 energy."�\bLastly, these buffs are only active in the Sync Challenge. If she gave any healing in the Titan Challenge, it would be wayyy too easy!"}\bBoosters give your Pokémon +1 to a stat (except Accuracy and Evasion) after they use a move, even if the move failed."Q\bAll of them use 1 energy and can't be upgraded further like Blessings can."l\bCrushers lowers one of the target's stats (except Accuracy and Evasion) by -1 after they're attacked."f\bAlso, they won't be effective in Titan Challenge; all opponents there are immune to stat drops."9\bI wish I could join the Fire Ash Discord Events..."`\bThrough those events, I could win high IV boosts or maybe rare shinies and legendaries..."\bShucks..."N\bI might have lost.... But my determination is still burning high!!!!!!!"A\rNurse Joy: Looks like your Pokémon need some patching up."R\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Get ready and take care now!"L\rOh, good! Your Pokémon are looking great now. Better luck next time!"\bOut of bounds, kiddo!"*\rThese challenges are an eye opener."]\rThat towering Inferno, shivering Sheer Cold. An overwhelming Draco Meteor coming next."R\rWhere do these trainers come from? Whoa... I wish I could be like them too.":\rConcierge Joi: Welcome to the Secret Grandeur Club!"\\rComing from other dimensions, numerous top-notch trainers have arrived for showdowns!"/\rPick your challenge - rewards await you!"Y\rYou may also look for me to return your Pokemon to you if you lose your challenge."\rAll the best!"3\rWelcome back! Here's your remaining Pokemon."#\rDon't give up! Do try again!"4Announcer: You're gonna quit now? Are you sure?"!\bAnnouncer: Please head up."\bHey \PN."g\bThis is where you are gonna be partnering up with someone of your choice, to take on other duos."r\bThe combination is endless and up to your decision. This also means victory is not up to your full control."\bExciting right?"Y\bHey, partner! Can I interest you in some moves? They don't have these anywhere else, you know.\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas,Dual Wingbeat, Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam,Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage, Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]" \bCome again! Or not. Hehe."\bAny other moves?\ch[98,-1,Burning Jealousy,Coaching,Corrosive Gas, Dual Wingbeat,Expanding Force,Flip Turn,Grassy Glide,Lash Out,Meteor Beam, Misty Explosion,Poltergeist,Rising Voltage,Scale Shot,Scorching Sands,Skitter Smack,Steel Roller,Terrain Pulse,Triple Axel]"0\bAnother worthy challenger comes and goes."Y\bI see your excitement and unwavering determination. You should have what it takes."U\bDon't give up, young man! Just like me. I've been here for ages now. Hohohoho."<PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE JUKEBOX MENU..."+WELCOME [\PN]! PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR BGM."\ch[77,-1,Default Beats]"a\ch[77,,Default Beats,Spring Violin,Summer Flute,Autumn Guitar,Winter Harmonica,Night Piano]"M\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep up yourself."L\rHave a break. Grab a cuppa joe. Take a quickie in the loo. Go for it!"C\rOnce you are ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"#\rWhat a bummer. I lost again.">\rIt's really hard to conquer them with just 3 Pokemon..."+\rTEACH ME. HOW DO I WIN AGAINST THEM?"T\bHey \PN, you chose the Gauntlet huh. So what would you like me to talk about?"�\bThis challenge is simple. Basically, it's a survival mode. Keep fighting your challengers till you fall. So don't be disheartened or sad that you lost. You did your very best."l\bBut making it neverending seems like no way out yea? So I kept the limit at 100. Good to know, right?"Z\bOne last tip, check with Nurse Joy from time to time, alright? Now get going! Shoo!"<\bLet me check......\nYour current win count is \v[81]."
\bOne. More. Match.\nAre you shaking in fear? Trembling with excitement? Or you are gonna strut out of this place with your head held high? You've done great nonetheless. :) Screenshot this and look for me in Discord, you are worthy of the role: [Gauntlet Maniac]!!!"�\bUrgh... I am tired of looking at your face now. Just kidding. Look at the time. How long has it been? Have you eaten? Had a bath? You are getting there real soon!"�\bSheesh, you are still here? You must have shown real determination to last till now. You should screenshot this moment and show it off!"�\bYou have passed the halfway mark! Congratulations! So what's this going to be? The end for you? Or you gonna keep going up to this seemingly... endless... cycle...?"s\bHonestly, you did well. This is a good number for dedicated players. Give yourself a pat on your back. Yeah!"Z\bAlright, you got so far! What are you still standing here for? Hmmmm? Taking a nap?"�\bOk, this is decent for casual players. I would like to thank you for challenging Gauntlet and making my efforts worthwhile. :)"�\bYou might be facing some struggles now. Maybe consider grinding more in Practice and Club? Redeem more goodies to boost your Pokemon!"U\bStop checking your win count when you can count them with one hand. Sheesh. :)"^\bStop checking your win count when you don't even need a hand to count it. Sheeeeesh. :)"`\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Let me explain how it works."w\bThe Club Challenge is really just a small taste of what's to come in other parts of the Grandeur Club. Hehehe..."�\bDepending on the difficulty you picked earlier, you will fight a certain amount of trainers. For Rookie, that's 3 Gym Leaders, for Veteran that's 4 Gym Leaders and an Elite 4 member and for Ace that's 5 Gym Leaders, 2 Elite 4 members and a "Champion"."?\bAt the end, talk to Hitsu for a reward for your efforts!"S\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Club Challenge. Want some tips?"�\bFirst off, you might want to consider using moves with a slightly lower base power but have more PP than the moves you currently have."y\bThat way, you don't run out of PP for a move and lose type coverage in the middle of a battle, which really sucks."\bSource? Trust me, mate."�\bNext, you should definitely consider giving your Pokémon a good spread of EVs. That way you're not leaving the opponent on 1 HP!"x\bYou might want to also consider using some status moves rather than just brute forcing your way through a battle."%\bThat's all from me, good luck!"&\bBoo. Oh well, good luck anyway."5Announcer: You are gonna quit now? Are you sure?"R\rAfter a tough time, I finally got through one of the Club challenges. Phew."d\rDon't mind me. I am just pondering about what Pokémon I should bring next for my challenges."T\bHi, this is the entrance for the PRACTICE CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"|\bAnd which region will you be challenging? \ch[98,-1,Kanto,Johto,Hoenn,Sinnoh,Unova,Kalos, Alola,Galar,Hisui,Frontier]"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Club Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Club Challenge."F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokemon looks really roughed up."Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, i am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"%\rHehe, desperate yea? Alrighty!"7\rAll's great now! Take care! Please come again!!!"H\rHey! You can't afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rAwwww, be careful out there. *wink*"U\bHehe, I keep getting paired up with the Champions! What a joke of a challenge."~\b... is what I would say if that wasn't a dream I had last night. I actually just get Gym Leaders as my choices. AHHHHH!"S\b<i>Sobs</i>. <i>Sobs</i>... My team of Rattatas... obliterated. Waaaaaaaaaa~"�\bNow this challenge, i would say is the MOST COMPLICATED CHALLENGE in the entire Grandeur Club. So listen carefully. Or you could just go and learn by stumbling, falling and tripping yourself up."�\bThis is basically a maze, a labyrinth, a penitentiary. You choose and enter 1 of the 6 entrances, and you gotta escape by collecting 5 keys. Keys will be given out to random trainers, so you know, you gotta defeat them to get the keys."�\bOnce you've gotten all 5 keys, all entrances are now exits, and you just gotta find your way out. Understand everything now? I wish you all the best. :)"{\bLuc-ker: Yo \PN! Here to take on the Titan Challenge? Can't wait to see your reaction to the trainers here, hehe. ;)"�\bIn this challenge specifically, you also won't be able to inflict your opponents with status conditions, flinch, trap or confuse them!"�\bLastly, cheese moves like Destiny Bond and Perish Song won't work here; Knock Off also won't knock off their items. Don't try them!"{\bSince I realised the the difficulty of the Titan Challenge was a mistake, I've given you some buffs to help you out."�\bHowever, your fainted mons will only receive 10% of their max HP regardless of whether or not you have a HP Restoration buff. So keep your mons alive!"i\bAlso, they won't be effective here in the Titan Challenge; all opponents are immune to stat drops."!\bFoul: Why hello there pal!"\bAre you lost?"�\bTook the wrong turn looking for the bathroom? Well don't you worry, just follow me and I will take you back to where you're supposed to be."9\bOh who am I kidding. We both know you're not lost."f\bThis is one of the most secure facilities in this dimension; people don't just get "lost" here."t\bYour luck seems to have run out now that I've found you before the other two, see, I'm not as nice as them..."!\bBut then again, I'm bored."\bEhhh, why not."~\bSee, it would be mean if I defeated you now, but wouldn't it be even meaner if I healed you, just to make you wipe out?"+\bLet me show you what I mean by that!"<\bNot too bad, maybe you do have some skills after all."L\bNow scram and make sure I don't catch you sneaking around here again!"d\bBut maybe leave a resume on your way out. We might need someone of your talent in the future."P\bWhat's up, feeling lost? A newcomer would be overwhelmed with this place."J\bLook for Luc, he will tell you what you to expect in Grandeur Club."a\bHow're you doin'? I hope you are not surprised by the trainers' standard in Grandeur Club."|\bLook for Luc from time to time to understand rules and regulations of various challenges. Re-evaluate your team if needed."K\bIf you are stuck, farm and grind. You will get there. MUAHAHAHAHAHA!""\rThis challenge is so weird."U\rI don't know if I'm holding my partner back, or if it's the other way round..."0\r*sighs* I guess it's all up to luck, huh?"'\bDid you complete the challenges?"<\bI see some trainers come out there from time to time."(\bI wonder what Pokémon they used."S\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Titan Challenge!"F\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your Pokémon look really roughed up."v\rVermint: Hello \PN, I hope you enjoy your stay here. Try not to think too much about our first encounter, okay?"W\rVermint: Hello \PN, I had foreseen that I would have to introduce myself to you."^\rMy true name is Vera. I created your wardrobe and I am also here to judge your resolve."-\rI hope this isn't a shock to you, \PN."bThe abyss is deep and dark. You shiver as you can feel overwhelming forces enamating from it."JYou almost blacked out. It would be a good idea to stay away from it."J\rNurse Joi: This is the Backstage, a place for you to prep yourself."B\rOnce you're ready, head to the top for your next challenge!"I\bDon't mind me, I'm just mentally preparing myself before going in."J\bI'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime, I'llwinthistime!"FAn ominous Vending Machine stares at you. Best not to go near it."=PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS ENEMY SYGNA BUFFS..."WELCOME [\PN]!"vYou can't seem to get the Vending Machine to work anymore. Maybe it can only be used before starting a challenge?"#The exit seems to be locked..."?\bThis is a great place to level up your Pokemon to Lv100!"A\bHitsukid made this challenge just for that reason in mind!"�\rI heard a rumour that once upon a time, there were no difficulties for this challenge and that trainers would stack on top of Nurse Joy."M\rTerrifying, right? I'm glad that it doesn't happen anymore, if it did."
\bAsh"\bLance"\bBrawly"c\bLuc-ker: Oh, you want to battle me at my full power? Fine, but don't say you weren't warned."G\bLuc: Too easy, huh? I lied - that wasn't actually my full power."�\bMy real master, Yhwach, gifted me with the shift V - The Visionary, turning my imagination into reality! That means I can throw at you whatever I can conjure and I simply haven't had enough to imagine yet."\bUntil next time!"Z\bLuc: Hehe, that's a taste of what's to come soon. Thanks for letting me go all-out!"MIt's a Vending Machine. Is it like all the other ones in the main lobby?"7PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS SYGNA BUFFS..."�YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION. \ch[98,-1,Buff shop,View active buffs,View unlocked buffs,Add buff, Remove active buff,Clear active buffs,Close menu]")YOU HAVE BOUGHT ALL BUFFS AVAILABLE."YOU HAVE NO ACTIVE BUFFS."%YOU HAVE NO MORE UNLOCKED BUFFS."ACTIVE BUFFS CLEARED."gOh dear, looks like you don't have enough Pokémon to battle. Talk to Nurse Joy to get patched up."#\bPsst! Want to know a secret?"i\bI heard that Luc-ker nearly went insane trying to get trainers from Pasio here for this challenge."e\bAnd oh boy did it work out for him. Now we have these monstrosities disguised as "challenges"."H\bThey're not even "challenges", they're just straight up bullying!"�\bI guess the one saving grace is the existence of blessings... an idea he got after playing far too much of a rougue-like mode in a certain game."\bHaha, your loss then."C\rDid you know that there's a way to get to the higher floors?"O\rI hear that only strong trainers or certain VIPs will have access to it."�\rHow do you know if you're strong? I heard another rumour that, if you get good in Club, and I mean <i>real good</i> in Club, they'll acknowledge you."7\rHope you will be one to get there. All the best!"X\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope the Duet Challenge is not giving you a tough time!"d\rApologies if you are looking for a heal. This service is not available in the Duet Challenge."G\rHey! You cant afford my service! Get blacked out and outta here!"*\rHmm... what blessings should I use?"}\rI could use "Assassin's Blessing" for that extra speed so that my Lucario has enough speed to outspeed almost everything..."�\bBut I also need it to hit hard enough, so I want "Warrior's Blessing"... or should I swap to a special set and use "Warlock's Blessing" to power up my Regieleki even further...?"�\rAh, but then I can't get Unflappable to deal with whatever <i>that<\i> is... ugh. Maybe just Lv 2 on one of my blessings then?"^\rHuh? You don't know what I'm talking about? Hahaha, you haven't lost to them, have you?"X\rYou're either really good, or you haven't been whooped yet. Either way, have fun!"5\bOnly authorized staffs are permitted to enter."1\ch[98,-1,Display your Staff Pass,Walk Away]"b\bOh, you are one of the staff here? You should have show me your pass earlier. Please enter."\bPlease leave. Thank you."�\bFoul: Hello! Glad to see that you are finally here. In case you don't recognise me, my name is Foul Play at A Garbodor Price, but my friends call me Foul."�\bI am one of the few people to be chosen here before you to test my strength against this place. And I can tell you from experience that you are gonna have a lot of fun, or not. It depends on you after all."q\bTonnes of huge experimental vessels containing floating specimens in colourful bubbly liquids can be seen."9\bMan, I love this challenge despite how hard it is."w\bThe different trainers you get to face, their unique gimmicks, their drip and even the blessings you get to use."\bIt's beautiful. :')"P\bHi, this is the entrance for the CLUB CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"K\bHi, this is the entry for MAYHEM CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your original bag back soon enough.">\bYou have a Backstage Pass. Let me tear that up for you."R\bHow strange. You don't seem to have a backstage pass. Try buying one again." \bPlease let me escort you."�\bFor this run, you'll have your bag, but you'll have a preset amount of items. Don't worry, you'll get your bag back soon enough."1\bIntriguing coloured-specimens can be seen."7\bOut of bou...... hmmmm? Let me answer this call.",\bYes sir? Yes. Yes. He is here. Roger."N\bApologies. You may enter and access the higher floor as of now. Please."8\bHope you're having fun in the Grandeur Club, \PN!"/\bWant to refresh yourself on a challenge?"T\bYo! I'm Luc-ker, nice to meet you, \PN! (The hyphen is important by the way.)"�\bHmm? How do I know your name? Ahahaha, don't worry about the specifics. By the way, you can call me Luc for short if my full name is too hard for you."o\bAnyway, I'm here to help you out by giving you some information on the challenges, as Hitsu wants me to."X\bYou'd better jot them down on a piece of paper, instead of just spamming confirm!"i\bThere's 6 main challenges to take on in the Grandeur Club. Which one would you like to know about?"~\ch[1,-1,Club Challenge, Practice Challenge, Gauntlet Challenge, Mayhem Challenge,Sync Challenge, Titan Challenge,Finish]"W\bThe Club Challenge - here, you can battle characters from the main series games."\bIf you can battle characters from the anime and Pokémon Adventures, then why not the same for the main series games as well?"w\bYou'll be facing Lv 90 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle. If you do well enough, you might get some... *ahem* privileges.",\bAnything else you would like to know?"b\bThe Practice Challenge. If the Club Challenge is too difficult for you, try this challenge!"\bSimilar to Club Challenge, but the Pokémon are at Lv 75 and hold no items, so it's a good place to grind your Pokémon!"}\bThe Gauntlet Challenge, the challenge that chucks trainers at you until your team drops (or until you defeat 150 trainers)."{\bYou will be facing Lv 100 Pokémon in a 3v3 battle, with benefits at certain intervals to help you build your win streak."�\bYour longest, most glorious run will be logged for you so you can boast in Discord with fellow players, so whip out the big guns!"x\bThe Mayhem Challenge - in this one, you battle with trainers in a full battles and they have all Lv 100 Pokémon."�\bIf you pay attention, you'll realise that even if you face the same trainer on next run, their team line-up is hardly the same!"~\bThat's because they're holding a pool of Pokémon awaiting for your arrival. You'll never know what's up their sleeves!"^\bThey have high IVs as well, so you'd better bring your best 6, because THIS IS MADNESS!"�\bThe Sync Challenge; you'll battle "Sygna Suit" trainers (and other outfits) from the hit mobile game "Pokémon Masters EX" in 3v3 triple battles."�\bTheir Pokémon may also have special gimmicks, for example not needing to recharge after using a move with high base power, or not being able to miss attacks."B\bYou'd better bring your lucky charm, the challenge is real!"�\bThe Titan challenge you'll be battling Sync Pokémon, also known as Titans, in a 6v1 triple battle. <s>This was made before Scarlet and Violet, way before they thought it was cool.</s>"}\bThey'll be retaining their gimmick from the Sync Challenge, but they're much tankier, and you can't rely on AOE moves."}\bHitsu's idea is this is to mimic the scenario of Quest Raids from certain RPG games. So ready up, and go for the head!"2\bPhew! Thanks for that. Good luck out there!"\bWhat the heck."q\bI took my Necrozma to the Hyper Trainer to max out its IVs. It has 252 EVs in Special Attack. It's Modest."j\bSO WHY THE HECK, AFTER ULTRA BURSTING, IS ITS Z-MOVE ONLY HITTING FOR 30-35% ON MISTY'S POKÉMON???"\bARGHHHHHH!"\bShow me your best!"O\bBrock: The world is huge. There are still many strong trainers like you."0\bI have faith that you will overcome them!"C\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN. Your team looks really roughed up."{\rThe unit behind me broke down, so that's no more healing for you for the rest of the challenge, for better or worse."!\rCome back again next time!"B\rThe unit is all charged up. Let's heal your team, shall we?"3\rAll's great now! Put your best foot out, ok?"g\rHehe, desperate yea? I could heal you up with the unit behind me, but it is still not ready yet."|YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE SELECT AN OPTION.\ch[98,-1,View active buffs,Other options?,Close menu]"iThe other options have been grayed out. Maybe they can only be accessed before starting a challenge?"\rSheeeeeeeesh."}\rEither these Titans have a ridiculous amount of health and/or defenses, or our damage is being reduced by an insane amount."N\rWelp. Either way, it sure feels like I'm facing a JRPG boss every time."<\bCongrats, you made it through the PRACTICE CHALLENGE!"@\bDepending on the difficulty selected, here's your reward."+\b1 GC Credit has been awarded to you.")\bDo compete again for more rewards!"c\bYou may exit by following the arrow sign; it's best not to loiter around this area. Alright?"?\bNo no no. No more rewards. But you can always try again?"8\bCongrats, you made it through the CLUB CHALLENGE!"-\b2 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b5 GC Credits have been awarded to you."-\b3 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b10 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b20 GC Credits have been awarded to you."<\bCongrats, you made it through the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE!"1\bDepending on your run, here's your reward.":\bCongrats, you made it through the MAYHEM CHALLENGE!".\b25 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b50 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b75 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the DUET CHALLENGE!".\b15 GC Credits have been awarded to you.".\b40 GC Credits have been awarded to you."8\bCongrats, you made it through the SYNC CHALLENGE!"2\b\v[61] GC Credits have been awarded to you."9\bCongrats, you made it through the TITAN CHALLENGE!"\\rHeh. No matter how many times you do this challenge, there are no two identical runs."c\rWell, ok. Maybe there is, but it's like a 0.000000000000000000000000000000000000001% chance."�\bLike, seriously. There are so many trainers and their teams might not even be the same each time, even if you face the same trainer."u\rAND it might not even be in the same order or rooms as in the previous run, even if the trainers are the same."=\bAh, the challenges here are way tougher than expected.""\bI am kinda bummed about it."(\bHow about you? Are you up for it?".\bHow's it going? Bet you're doing great!"B\bYou will overcome and make your way back here again. Right?"B\bHmm. It's so hard to formulate a strategy for each trainer."�\bThing is, there's no such thing as a "perfect lead". You could lead off with a Ferrothorn and it would do amazing against Marlon, but then it would get one shot from any of Flint's Pokémon."o\bAnd then you'd have to waste items... or even worse, have one less Pokémon for the rest of the battles."9\rWow, this is delicious! One more on the go please!"e\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you are taking this chance to grind your Pokemon up to tip-top!"E\r..........hope you are not coming here for a quick heal, yeah?"_\rWow... Erm, this service is not available in the Practice Challenge. Apologies for that."$\rDo your very best... alright?"8\rNurse Joy: Great! You go and get those wins, \PN!"/\bThis is inhumane. I might call it a day."*\bI was fired from my job last month."�\bNow I have nothing better to do than grind this. My longest win streak is 70... healing is a lot less frequent the higher you go."]\bHi, this is the entrance for the GAUNTLET CHALLENGE. Your highest win count is \v[93]."\bWould you like to enter?">\bThis curry dish is just like my challenges in the Club."\bKICKIN' my ass... Sobs."9\bBwahahahaha. I... am having shivers on this floor.";PLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS THE REWARD MENU..."aWELCOME [\PN]! YOU HAVE \v[80] CREDITS IN YOUR ACCOUNT. PLEASE CHOOSE YOUR REWARD TO REDEEM."�\ch[98,-1,***SPECIAL OFFER DEAL***, Enhancements (1 Credit),Alterfication (3 Credits), Lounge BGM Pack (10 Credits),Gems (1 Credit), Held Items,Credit-Money Exchange]"o\ch[75,-1, Code: Luck (2 Credits), VIP Backstage Pass (5 Credits), Grandeur Club Staff Pass (500 Credits)]"(PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!">YOU HAVE INSUFFICIENT CREDIT. PLEASE COME BACK NEXT TIME.""REDEEM SUCCESSFUL! THANK YOU!"0BACKSTAGE PASS NOT FOR SALE YET! THANK YOU!".BACKSTAGE PASS ALREADY BOUGHT! THANK YOU!"7YOU ALREADY OWN A STAFF PASS. COME BACK NEXT TIME."c\ch[75,-1,Intensity Tonic, Vigor Serum, Dense Extract,Hidden Stimulant,Apex Vaccine,Bolt Brew]"U\ch[75,-1,Code: Breath,Code: Grim,Code: Wall,Code: Storm,Code: Dome,Code: Shine]"WLOUNGE BGM PACK ALREADY BOUGHT AND DOWNLOADED! PLEASE COLLECT YOUR PAD! THANK YOU!"=LOUNGE BGM PACK DOWNLOADED INTO GRANDEUR PAD! THANK YOU!"L\ch[98,-1,1 Credit,2 Credits,3 Credits,5 Credits,8 Credits,10 Credits ]"d\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challenge. Let me explain how it works."�\bThe Practice Challenge is essentially an easier version of the Club Challenge so that you can level up your Pokémon in preparation for it. In other words, we designed this challenge for grinding."V\bHey \PN, I see you've decided to take on the Practice Challnge. Want some tips?"Z\bSorry, you need at least 3 Pokémon that are able to battle for the Sync challenge."P\bHi, this is the entrance for the SYNC CHALLENGE. Would you like to enter?"S\bPlease do not disturb me. I need to formulate a strategy for the challenges."APLEASE INSERT YOUR GC PAD TO ACCESS YOUR GRANDEUR RECORDS..."CWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club]"$Your Practice Records is empty." Your Club Records is empty."XWHAT RECORDS WOULD YOU LIKE TO CHECK? \ch[98,-1,Practice,Club,Gauntlet,Duet,Mayhem]"$Your Gauntlet Records is empty." Your Duet Records is empty.""Your Mayhem Records is empty."T\rNurse Joy: Good day, \PN! Hope you will have a good time in Mayhem Challenge!"Y\rNurse Joy: If you wanna get patched up, I am gonna need to charge you $1000000. :D"O\rI heard there are many more challengers from around the world have here."I\rThis will allow me to know where I stand in my journey to the top!"Yes"No"Rookie"Veteran"Ace"Master"Challenge"Win Counts"Cancel"Backstage"	Yes?"No!Iu;␀�
